2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Decatur Daily Democrat, Adams County, IN , Tuesday April , 17, 1973 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT                   James Muselman and Kerry Egly died in accident on U.S. highway 27
2 CONT
2 CONT             The fifth and sixth Adams county highway traffic fatalities of 1973 were recorded Monday afternoon when two Berne teenagers lost their lives in a car-semi collision tow miles north of that city on rain slicked US 27
2 CONT
2 CONT             Pronounced dead on arrival at Lutheran hospital in Fort Wayne by the Allen county coroner were James H. Muselman, 17, of Berne, driver of the car, and Kerry D. Egly, 17, also of Berne, a passenger.  Coroner Dr. Gordon 
2 CONC Franke said both died as  a result of massive head injuries…..
2 CONT
2 CONT             The teenagers were members of the South Adams high school golf team and were returning to Berne from a scheduled golf match in Decatur with Bellmont.  The match had been cancelled due to rain…….
2 CONT
2 CONT                                                 Funerals Thursday
2 CONT
2 CONT             Funeral services will be held Thursday at the First Missionary Church at Berne.  The James H. Muselman funeral will be held at 10 a.m. and the Kerry D. Egly rites are scheduled for 2 p.m.  Rev. C.E. Prosser will offici
2 CONC ate.  Burial will be in the M.R.E. Cemetery. Friends may call at the Yager funeral home after 2 p.m. Wednesday.
2 CONT
2 CONT             James H. Muselman, a senior at South Adams high school, was born on July 9, 1955, in Decatur, the son of Carl and Marilyn Smith-Muselman, and was a member of the South Adams golf team.  He was a member of the First Mis
2 CONC sionary church.
2 CONT
2 CONT             Surviving are the parents and grandparents, Mr. and Mrs. C.H. Muselman and Mrs. Lester Smith, and two brothers, John and Tom, both at home.
2 CONT
2 CONT             Kerry D. Egly, a junior at South Adams high school, was born on Nov. 6, 1955, in Decatur, the son of Albert and Norma Jean Inniger-Egly, and was a member of the South Adams basketball and golf team.  He was a member of
2 CONC  the First Missionary church.
2 CONT
2 CONT             Surviving are his parents and grandparents, Mr. and Mrs. Amos Inniger and Mrs. Valentine Egly, and two sisters, Kendra and Kelly, both at home.
2 CONT (Contributed by Janice Vasilovski)
2 CONT **
2 CONT
2 CONT KERRY D. EGLY    Date of Birth:  November 6, 1968 (sic:  1955)Date of Death:  April 16, 1973; Age: 17    SERVICES FROM First Missionary Church, Thurs. April 19, 1973 2:00 p.m.FINAL RESTING PLACE:  M.R.E. Cemetery, grave 7, Lot 21,
2 CONC  Sec 5 – 4th Add.    Arrangements by Yager Funeral Home, Berne, Indiana Berne (IN) Library Heritage Room MRE Obits 1973-1984, image #012 Transcribed by Joey Pedigo* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/55390650/kerry-d-
