1 NOTE {geni:about_me} SON OF: Johannes Lengacher, Sr and Anna (Knecht) Lengacher 
2 CONT
2 CONT married on November 5, 1855 to Mary Lengacher born February 15, 1833, France and died August 5, 1890, Allen Co., In
2 CONT
2 CONT They were the parents of 9 children all born in Allen Co., Indiana: 1. a stillborn daughter born 1856 2. Anna Lengacher born April 20, 1857 died September 20, 1932 married to: Michael Zehr born September 14, 1853 and died March 19
2 CONC , 1907 3. Samuel Lengacher born January 24, 1859 died November 24, 1893, Montgomery, Indiana married to: Anna (Leichty) Graber born January 24, 1860. 4. Mary Lengacher born July 25, 1860 died September 9, 1928 Grabill, Indiana mar
2 CONC ried to: Joseph Graber born July 8, 1858, Allen Co., In died June 19, 1933 5. Elizabeth Lengacher born December 24, 1861, and died  married to: John A Miller born  and died 6. John Lengacher III born June 20, 1864  died September 
2 CONC 20,1944 married to: Louisa Graber born February 18, 1868 of Daviess co., In died July 16, 1945 7. Rosa Lengacher born February 9, 1867 - died May 10,1936 married to: Peter Arnold Steury born August 26,1858, Switzerland and died Se
2 CONC ptember 27, 1938 8. Fannie Lengacher born January 22, 1869, Allen Co., In died June 13, 1930, Allen co., In married to: Victor Delagrange, Jr born June 3,1861, Allen Co., In died December 4, 1920, Allen co., In 9. Magdalena Lengac
2 CONC her born December 15, 1877, Allen Co., Indiana - died March 18, 1942,  married to: John G Wittmer born November 19, 1876, and died June 20, 1931
2 CONT
2 CONT Johannes Lengacher was born March 26, 1830, the oldest son among the 8 children of Johannes Lengacher, Sr., and his wife Anna Knecht. Johannes, Jr., was the 1st member of the family to emigrate to America. It was after his arrival
2 CONC  in Ohio, and his stay in the home of his uncle Christian Lengachers, that Johannes, Jr., learned to know his cousin Mary. Meanwhile, they had moved to Allen County, Indiana, and it was there on November 5, 1855 that Johannes, Jr.
2 CONC , and Mary were married. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They were the parents of 9 children in all, but only 8 grew to adulthood and entered marriage. 
2 CONT
2 CONT According to his passport, John Lengacher was a farmer, 24 years old at the time of his migration, 5 feet, 5 inches tall, black hair, brown eyes, a medium nose and a large mouth. His chin was round and his face was long. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Johannes Lengacher, Jr., and his wife Mary both died in the year 1890. Johannes passed away March 29, 1890 at the age of 60. His wife Mary died August 5, 1890 at the age of 57. They were buried in the Amish Cemetery near Grabill, 
2 CONC Row 3, North Side. 
2 CONT
2 CONT .. Find A Grave Memorial ID 79962740 
