2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 14 FEB 1903
2 PLAC Geneva, Hartford Twp., Adams County, IN
2 ADDR
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 7 FEB 1960
2 PLAC Adams County Memorial Hosp., Decantur, IN
2 ADDR
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Handwritten-Mon. Feb. 8, 1960
2 CONT
2 CONT ?? Man Dies Sunday At County Hospital
2 CONT
2 CONT Valentine A. Egly Dies After Week's Illness; Rites Wed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Valentine A. Egly, 56, of 151 1/2 West Main Street and widely known throughout this community, died at 12:45 p.m. at the Adams County Memorial Hospital in Decatur.  Death was attributed to a cerebral hemorrhage.  He suffered a str
2 CONC oke Saturday morning, January 30, and was admitted to the hospital.
2 CONT
2 CONT He responded to treatment but suffered another stroke last week and had been unconscious since.  Egly had been in ill health since Sept. 2, 1951, when he suffered his first stroke.  He and his family lived in Kirkland Township at 
2 CONC that time.  He had not been able to do any heavy work since then but seemed to be making steady improvement until he was stricken a week ago Saturday.
2 CONT
2 CONT A lifelong resident of Adams County, Egly was employed as a painter at International Harvester Company in Fort Wayne until he became ill.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a native of Hartford Township and was born February 14, Valentine's Day, 1903, the son of Abraham and Leah Stucky Egly.  He was married to Ida Klopfenstein, Dec. 8, 1922, at Hillsdale, Michigan.  The family moved to Berne s
2 CONC everal years ago.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving is the wife; two sons, Lester E. Egly, Berne R. R. 1; Albert D. Egly, Berne; four daughters, Mrs. Gerald (Violet) Ringenberg, Cleveland, Ohio; Mrs. Paul (Choletta) Erdel, Ecuador, South America; Mrs. Milton (Glennavere) 
2 CONC Wong, Fort Wayne and Mrs. David H. (Carolyn) Nussbaum, Berne; 14 grandchildren; two brothers, Jesse Egly, Danville, Illinois and Harve Egly, Berne, and a sister, Mrs. Benjamin Sprunger, Berne, now vacationing in Florida.
2 CONT
2 CONT Two brothers, Simon and Chris Egly, preceded in death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Egly was a member of the West Missionary Church where services will be held at 2 p.m. Wednesday, Rev. Robert Magary officiating.  Mr. Egly was a member of this church. Burial will be in M.R.E. Cemetery.  Friends may call at th
2 CONC e Yager Funeral Home after 7 p.m. today.
2 CONT
2 CONT Adams County, Indiana Historical Museum "Jan1958-Dec1960"
2 CONT Image 74
2 CONT Transcribed by Janice Vasilovski* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/55390699/valentine-albert-egly Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 16 2023, 6:32:23 UTC''
