2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 2 DEC 2007
2 PLAC Berne, Adams, Indiana, United States
2 ADDR
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Carolyn J. Nussbaum, 73, of Berne, Indiana passed away at 12:25 p.m. Sunday, December 2, 2007 in the Swiss Village located in Berne.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Carolyn was born on December 3, 1933 in Adams County, Indiana the daughter of the late Valentine Egly and the late Ida (Klopfenstein) Egly. Carolyn married David H. Nussbaum on July 18, 1953 and he survives.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Carolyn was member of the West Missionary Church and had been a former employee of the First Bank of Berne as a teller. Carolyn enjoyed traveling and loved her family.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Carolyn is survived by her husband, David H. Nussbaum of Berne, Indiana; daughter, Kim (Roger) Young of Berne, Indiana; son, Bradley (Deborah) Nussbaum of Ft.Wayne, Indiana; brother, Lester (Carol) Egly of Travelers Rest, South C
2 CONC arolina; sister, Violet (Rev. Gerald) Ringenberg of Woodburn, Indiana; sister, Glenna (Milton) Wong of Ft. Wayne, Indiana; and four grandchildren: Erica (Marcel) Guevara of Mishawaka, Indiana, Natalie Young of Berne, Indiana, Loga
2 CONC n and Tiffany Nussbaum, of Ft. Wayne, Indiana.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Carolyn was preceded in death by a brother, Albert Egly and a sister, Chloetta Erdel.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Funeral services will be held at 10:00 a.m. Wednesday, December 5, 2007 in the West Missionary Church with the Rev. Keith Rupp officiating. Interment will follow in the M.R.E. Cemetery in Berne, Indiana.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Family and friends will be received from 2-5 and 6-8 p.m. Tuesday, December 4, 2007 in the Yager-Kirchhofer Funeral Home, Berne, Indiana and from 9-10 a.m. at the church on Wednesday. Preferred memorials are to church missions or
2 CONC  Swiss Village.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Yager-Kirchhofer Funeral Home online obit
