1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Samuel Lengacher was born January 24, 1859 in Allen co., In to Johannes Lengacher, Jr and Mary (Lengacher) Lengacher. He was the older of their 2 sons, Samuel was 21 on November 11, 1880 when he married Anna Liecht
2 CONC y Graber , the widow of Jacob Graber of Allen Co., Indiana. About 1886 the Lengachers moved to Daviess County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel was a man 6 feet tall in his stocking feet. Family tradition has it that Samuel and his brother John left Allen County, Indiana because of church problems there, the details of which we are ingnorant. Together, the brothers
2 CONC  bought 38.61 acres from Charles Padgett, Jr on October 22,1886. They paid $2300. for this property in section 4 of Barr Township. East. On July 30, 1889 John sold his share to Samuel for $1,200.00
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel and Anna (Liechty) Lengacher were parents of 5 children when tragedy struck and the family in November 24, 1893. A granddaughter, Mrs Peter Yoder wrote this account
2 CONT
2 CONT Grandfather was only sick from one morning till the next noon. He with his brother John left early that morning to go north to cut logs. On the way he got very sick. They went in tothe house of a Mr Wade where Levi Grabers live no
2 CONC w. Mr Wade went with his wagon to get Grandmother. Apparently he died from a burst appendicitis. He had such hard cramps.
2 CONT
2 CONT Two months after the death of Samuel Lengacher, a daughter was born to his widow. The little girl was named Caroline. Mrs Lengacher married a 3rd time to Peter C Graber.
2 CONT
2 CONT ... Find A Grave Memorial ID 80744189 
2 CONT
