1 NAME Abraham /Egly/
2 GIVN Abraham
2 _MARNM Egly
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Evangelical Mennonite Church Cemetery, Berne, Adams County, Indiana, USA
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 7 FEB 1862
2 ADDR
3 CITY Hartford Township
3 STAE Indiana
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 28 NOV 1938
2 ADDR
3 CITY Hartford Township
3 STAE Indiana
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From the Berne Witness 
2 CONT Berne, Indiana(Adams County)
2 CONT Wednesday, November 30, 1938 
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham Egly, 76, Died of Infirmities
2 CONT
2 CONT Early Tues. A.M. Final Rites for Retired Farmer, Church Worker, Thursday P. M. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham Egly, 76, prominent Hartford township retired farmer and church worker, died Thursday morning at 3:50 o'clock. He had been in failing health for many years and was at the point of death for several days. Cause of his demis
2 CONC e which took place on his farm four miles southwest of Berne, was attributed to infirmities. He had suffered a paralytic stroke in 1926 but bore his affliction uncomplainingly. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The deceased was a son of the late Bishop Henry and Catherine Goldsmith Egly and was born on the farm where death occurred, on February 7, 1862. On September 23, 1883 the marriage to Leah Stucky took place. Six children were born 
2 CONC to the union. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving with the sorrowing widow are: Simon of Ft. Wayne, Jesse of Forest, Illinois, Mrs. Ben (Amanda) Sprunger, Harve of Berne and Valentine of Monroe. One son, Chris, preceded three years ago. Four brothers, Jacob, Henry, Samu
2 CONC el and Joseph and one sister, Magdalena Schenbeck, preceded.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Mr. Egly was a very active member of the West Missionary church prior to his illness serving the church as deacon, trustee, treasurer and chorister for many years.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/61419236/abraham
2 CONC -egly Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 16 2023, 6:37:16 UTC''
