1 NAME Leah /Stuckey/
2 GIVN Leah
2 SURN Stuckey
2 _MARNM Egly
1 SEX F
1 BURI
2 PLAC Evangelical Mennonite Church Cemetery, Berne, Adams County, Indiana, USA
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 20 NOV 1862
2 ADDR
3 CITY French Township
3 STAE Indiana
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 2 MAR 1939
2 ADDR
3 CITY Dalton
3 STAE Georgia
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} (Adams County, Indiana Historical Society, 1939 Scrapbook)
2 CONT
2 CONT (Handwritten date:  Thursday, March 2, 1939)
2 CONT
2 CONT TELEGRAM TELLS OF DEATH OF MRS. ABE EGLY
2 CONT Passes Away Following Accident and Heart Attack This A.M.
2 CONT
2 CONT                 "Dalton, Ga."
2 CONT       "Mother at rest 9:42 A.M.  Stop  Will arrive at Berne on Friday noon train  Stop notify others.  Amanda."
2 CONT
2 CONT    The above telegram was received this noon by Harvey Egly, bringing the message of the death of his mother, Mrs. Abe Egly, at Dalton, Ga.  It was sent by Mrs. Ben Sprunger, who had been at her bedside following the auto accident
2 CONC  of the party from Berne en route to St. Petersburg, Fla., consisting of Mr. and Mrs. Ben Sprunger, Mrs. Daniel Stucky and Mrs. Abe Egly, the deceased.  The accident occurred on February 21.
2 CONT    In that mishap two of the passengers received serious injuries, namely Ben Sprunger and Mrs. Egly, both of whom had to be taken to a hospital at Dalton, Ga.
2 CONT    A few days ago a message was received here that Mrs. Egly had suffered a heart attack, but that she was rallying nicely and resting easy.  According to the telegram, Mrs. Egly passed away Thursday forenoon at 9:42, at the Hamil
2 CONC ton Memorial hospital, Dalton, Ga.
2 CONT    Mrs. Abraham Egly, nee Leah Stucky, was born in French township, Adams County, Indiana as the daughter of Christian and Fannie Moser Stucky, on November 20, 1862, thus bringing her age to 76 years, 3 months and 10 days.  Fifty-
2 CONC five years ago she was married to Abraham Egly, who preceded her in death only a short time ago, passing away on November 29, 1938.  She spent all her life in this county.  She was a faithful member of the Missionary church west o
2 CONC f Berne.
2 CONT    Mrs. Egly is survived by the following children:  Mrs. Ben (Amanda) Sprunger of Berne;  Valentine Egly of Monroe;  Simon Egly of Ft. Wayne;  Harvey Egly of Berne, and Jesse Egly of Forrest, Illinois.  One son, Christian, preced
2 CONC ed her in death.
2 CONT    Besides the above, the following sisters remain:  Mrs. Peter N. Moser,  Mrs. J. C. Schindler,  and Mrs. Adam Augsburger, all of Berne, and Mrs. Levi Klopfenstein of Woodburn.  One sister and five brothers preceded her in death.
2 CONT    No funeral service arrangements had been made at the time of going to press.  It is expected that the entire party now at Dalton, Ga., will return tomorrow with the body of Mrs. Egly.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/mem
2 CONC orial/61419275/leah-egly Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 16 2023, 6:37:16 UTC''
