1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Handwritten-Wed. April 4, 1956
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon Egly, 70, Dies Tuesday At Fort Wayne
2 CONT
2 CONT Hartford Township Native to Be Buried Here Friday
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon Egly, 70, 3122 S. Harrison Street, Fort Wayne, a native of this community, died at 11:45 a.m. Tuesday at the Lutheran Hospital in Fort Wayne. He was a patient in the hospital two days. Mr. Egly suffered a stroke Sunday morni
2 CONC ng and never regained consciousness. He had been in good health previously.
2 CONT
2 CONT Before his retirement, Mr. Egly had been employed in the shipping department of the International Harvester Company for nine years. He moved to Fort Wayne a number of years ago from this community. He was born in Hartford Township
2 CONC , Dec. 19, 1885, the son of Abe and Leah Stucky Egly. His wife was the former Sarah Yoder and she preceded in death one year ago today. While living in this community Mr. Egly was a farmer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are two daughters, Miss Juanita Egly, at home, and Mrs. R. E. Dunlap, Fort Wayne; two grandchildren; a sister, Mrs. Ben Sprunger, Berne; three brothers, Jesse Egly, Danville, Illinois, and Harve and Valentine Egly of Ber
2 CONC ne. A daughter, Ruth, a son Merle, and a brother, Chris, preceded in death.
2 CONT
2 CONT The body was taken to the D. O. McComb and Son Funeral Home in Fort Wayne where friends may call after 7:00 p.m. today. Services will be held at 1:00 p.m. Friday at the funeral home, Rev. Cornelius Vlot officiating. Burial will be
2 CONC  in the M.R.E. Cemetery west of Berne. Mr. Egly was a member of the First Missionary Church in Fort Wayne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Adams County, Indiana Historical Museum"1955 Mar-April 1958" Scrapbook
2 CONT Image 42
2 CONT Transcribed by Janice Vasilovski
