1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mrs. Amanda Sprunger, 89, of Swiss Village, Berne, died Saturday at 8:15 p.m. at the Adams County Memorial Hospital.  She had been in ill health for six months.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a member of the First Mennonite Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Adams County on June 22, 1889, she was the daughter of Abraham and Leah Stuckey-Egly, and was married to John Hirschy.  She later married Ben Sprunger and both husbands preceded her in death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include a daughter-in-law, Mrs. Viola Moser, Berne; two grandchildren and six great-grandchildren.  Five brothers preceded her in death.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/32858104/amanda-m-sprunger Find A 
