1 BURI
2 PLAC MRE Cemetery, Berne, Adams County, Indiana, USA
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 19 NOV 1891
2 PLAC Geneva, Adams County, IN
2 ADDR
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 12 JUN 1976
2 PLAC Berne, Adams County, Indiana
2 ADDR
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Harvey Egly
2 CONT
2 CONT Harvey Egly, 84, longtime Water Commissioner for the City of Berne of 356 Dearborn Street, Berne, died at 10:45 a.m. Saturday at his home. Death was attributed to complications following several strokes. He had been in ill health 
2 CONC for the past two years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Egly was employed as a young man by the Pearl Oil Company as a gas bulk truck driver. He later served for approximately 20 years as Water Commissioner for the City of Berne and in later years was self employed as a painter. He
2 CONC  was retired.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Hartford Township on September 19, 1891, to Abraham and Leah Stucky Egly. He was married in Adams county in May of 1913 to Adele who died in 1974.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are one daughter, Mrs. Homer C. (Jean) Augsburger of Berne and one son, Carl H. of 4315 Marquette Dr., Fort Wayne; one brother, Jesse Egly of Danville, Illinois and one sister, Mrs. Ben (Amanda) Sprunger of Swiss Village
2 CONC ; three grandchildren and four great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be conducted at 3:00 p.m. today at the Yager Funeral Home in Berne with Rev. Wilson Bixler officiating. Burial will follow in the MRE Cemetery. Friends may call at the funeral home until time of services.
2 CONT
2 CONT Berne(IN) Library Heritage Room
