0 @I6000000195133273902@ INDI
1 NAME Christian Henry /Egly/
2 GIVN Christian Henry
2 SURN Egly
2 _MARNM Egly
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Greenwood Cemetery, Linn Grove, Indiana, United States
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 30 JUN 1897
2 PLAC Geneva, Adams, Indiana, United States
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 12 JUN 1935
2 PLAC Decatur, Adams, Indiana, United States
2 ADDR
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The deceased was born in Hartford township, June 30, 1897, a son of Abraham and Leah Stuckey Egly.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Egly was married to Miss Helen French, April 28, 1917.  Surviving are the wife, the parents of Hartford township, and three children, Robert, 16, Donald Douglas, 12, and Max, 8.  The following brothers and sisters survive: Sim
2 CONC on, Fort Wayne; Jesse, Forest, Ill.; Harve and Mrs. Ben (Amanda) Sprunger, Berne, and Valentine, of near Monroe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary
2 CONT Bluffton, Indiana Evening News Banner
2 CONT Thursday, June 13, 1935 – P1C7
2 CONT
2 CONT Christian H. Egly Answers Summons
2 CONT
2 CONT Nottingham Township Man Dies At Decatur Hospital Of Complications
2 CONT
2 CONT Christian H. Egly, 37, Nottingham township farmer, who at one time was associated with his brother, Harve Egly, in the garage business at Petroleum, died at 11:23 Wednesday night at the Adams county hospital, Decatur.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had been in poor health since January. A few weeks ago he was taken to the hospital for an operation. Physicians found that he was suffering from a rupture of the bowel. He rallied following the operation, but a few days ago de
2 CONC veloped pneumonia. His weakened condition made it impossible for him to successfully combat this additional complication.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Hartford township, Adams county, Jan. 30, 1897, a son of Abraham and Leah Stucky Egly. His marriage to Miss Helen French took place on April 28, 1917.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving besides the parents and the widow are three sons, Robert, 16; Don Douglas, 12, and Max 8. Four brothers and one sister surviving are Simon Egly, Fort Wayne; Mrs. Ben Sprunger and Harve Egly, of Berne; Jesse Egly, Forest,
2 CONC  Ill., and Valentine Egly, near Monroe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following the death of his mother-in-law, Mrs. J. D. French, he and his wife resided on the French farm in Nottingham township. He was a brother-in-law of Deputy Sheriff Fleming French, this city, and was a member of the Bluffton 
2 CONC Moose lodge.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held at 9:30 Saturday morning at the home in Nottingham township and at 10 o'clock at the Old Salem Evangelical church, west of Linn Grove. Burial will be in the Greenwood cemetery.
2 CONT
