1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Son of, Joseph A. and Anna L. Schwartz Hilty. Husband of Martha J. ShetNews-Sentinel, The (Fort Wayne, IN) - Saturday, August 26, 2000
2 CONT  Deceased Name: Joseph A. Hilty Monroe - 1925-2000
2 CONT  Joseph A. Hilty, 75, of Monroe, a retired farmer and carpenter, died Thursday, Aug. 24, 2000, at Caylor-Nickel Medical Center in Bluffton. The Adams County native was a member of Old Order Amish Church. Surviving are his wife, Ma
2 CONC rtha J.; sons Dan M. of Denver, Colo., and Henry M. and Elmer M., both of Monroe; daughters Mandy Hershberger of Apple Creek, Ohio, Annie Wickey and Martha Schwartz, both of Berne, Barbara Graber of Geneva and Elma Schwartz of Mon
2 CONC roe; a brother, Elmer A. of Monroe; sisters Maryann Girod, Lovina Shetler and Melinda Hilty, all of Monroe, and Mandy Shetler and Emma Schwartz, both of Berne; 71 grandchildren; and 42 great-grandchildren. Services are 9 a.m. Mond
2 CONC ay at the family residence, 130 W., 200 S., Monroe, with calling from 10 a.m. to 9 p.m. today and also from 9 a.m. to 9 p.m. Sunday, all at the residence. Burial will be at Schwartz Cemetery, Monroe. Information provided by Yager-
2 CONC Kirchhofer Funeral Home, Berne, 1-219-589-3101. ler. Cause of death, cancer.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
