1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Fred D. Schlabach, 80, of Arthur died 2:40 a.m. Thursday, (Dec. 24, 1987) in his home.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be 11:30 a.m. Saturday in family's residence. McMullin-Young Funeral Home, Sullivan, is in charge of arrangements. Burial will be in Yoder Cemetery, Arthur.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Schlabach was born in Garrett County, Md., son of Daniel and Abbie Schlabach. He was a retired farmer and bee keeper. He was a member of Old Order of Amish Faith. He married Mary Yoder in 1928. She died in 1968. He later marri
2 CONC ed Mattie Yoder in 1971. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are his wife; sons, Louis of Sullivan; Willard, Daniel, Eli and Harley, all of Arthur; daughters, Mrs. Ben (Lena) Schrock of Arcola; Mrs. Jacob (Abbie) Beachey of Ludington, Mich.; Mrs. Harvey (Sadie) Plank of Arcola; Mr
2 CONC s. Melvin (Annie Ellen) Otto of Arthur; Fannie Marie Schlabach of Arthur; stepson, John Yoder of Middlebury, Ind.; sisters, Katie Ann Kauffman of Arthur; Alma Yoder of Lovington; Mary Ellen Schlabach of Arcola; 64 grandchildren; 4
2 CONC 4 great-grandchildren; two step-grandchildren; two great-step-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT One brother, one sister, two grandchildren, one great-grandchild preceded him in death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Herald & Review (Decatur, Illinois) 
2 CONT Fri, Dec 25, 1987 - page 1.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/177231266/fred_d_schlabach Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 2 2024, 1:46:11 UTC''
