2 PLAC Olive Cemetery, Wakarusa, Elkhart County, Indiana, USA
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 10 AUG 1899
2 PLAC Haven, Reno, Kansas, United States
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 JUN 1957
2 PLAC Howard Township, Cass, Michigan, United States
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} David S Schrock
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st married Mattie Yoder Schrock, daughter of Noah Yoder & his wife Barbara Bontrager Yoder
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd married 1952 Jane Stackowski Schrock Puchala, son of Adalbert Puchala & his wife Josephine Chrabaszcz Puchala
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane married 1965 Daniel Puchala, son of Adalbert Puchala & his wife Josephine Chrabaszcz Puchala
2 CONT
2 CONT *********************
2 CONT
2 CONT The father of three Wakarusa residents was killed Saturday night in an auto accident near Niles, Mich.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was David Schrock, 57, of South Bend, who moved there from Wakarusa in 1943. Critically injured was Frank Jenczewski, 52, also of South Bend, the only other occupant of the car.
2 CONT
2 CONT Police said the car rolled over on M-60 six miles east of Niles. It struck a guard rail before halting in a field. Police have not determined who was driving. Mr Schrock was pinned beneath the wrecked car. Jenczewski was found abo
2 CONC ut 50 feet away.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Hutchinson, Kan, Aug 10, 1899, Mr Schrock married the former Jane Stackowski in South Bend Nov 23, 1952. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the father of Edward Schrock, Mrs Orval Beck, and Miss Mary Louise Schrock, all of Wakarusa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Other survivors are the widow five other children, David and Robert both at home, Mrs Delbert Kurtz and Mrs Gene Bontrager, both of Goshen, and Mrs Lowell Weaver of Nottowa, Mich; three brothers, Mose of Goshen, John of South Bend
2 CONC , and Tobias of LaJunta, Colo; and a sister, Mrs Levi Miller of Jamesport, Mo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held at 2 pm Tuesday in the Welsheimer funeral home at South Bend, with burial in Olive cemetery north of here. The Rev Simon Gingerich was in charge.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wakarusa Tribune 12 June 1957* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/69586304/david-s-schrock Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 7 2020, 22:44:16 UTC''
