2 DATE 1 SEP 1956
2 ADDR
3 CITY Bluffton
3 STAE Ohio
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} MRS. D. N. CASBON
2 CONT      Mrs. Kathryn Claudon, 89, widow of D. N. Claudon, a former Valparaiso resident, died at 3 a.m. today at the home of a daughter, Mrs. Elmer Vercler, in Bluffton, O., with whom she had lived for the past five years.
2 CONT      She was born in Geneva, Ind., Oct. 4, 1866, the daughter of Henry and Kathryn Egly. She was married to D. N. Claudon March 1, 1891, in Gridley, Ill. He preceded her in death July 7, 1947.
2 CONT      Surviving are five daughters, Mrs. Albert Morehead of New York City, Mrs. Ray Bloch of New York City, Mrs. Oliver Lugibill of Springfield, Ill., Mrs. Clarence Diller of Bluffton, and Mrs. Vercler; two sons, Jess D. Claudon an
2 CONC d Joseph H. Claudon, of Valparaiso; 20 grandchildren and 24 great-grandchildren.
2 CONT      In addition to her husband, five brothers and one sister and her parents preceded her in death. 
2 CONT      Services will be held at 2:30 p.m. Tuesday at the First Methodist church in Valparaiso. The Rev. Harvey J. Kieser of Indianapolis and the Rev. Charles M. Smith will officiate jointly. Burial will be at Graceland cemetery, and
2 CONC  the grandchildren will serve as pallbearers.
2 CONT      Friends may call from 4 p.m. Monday until noon Tuesday at Bartholomew Funeral home.
2 CONT
2 CONT --The Vidette-Messenger of Porter County
2 CONT (Valparaiso, IN), Sat., Sep. 1, 1956, Pg. 2* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/74782206/kathryn-e-claudon Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 16 2023, 6:42:23 UTC
