2 CONT   Native of this community died at Ft. Wayne after day's illness
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Sarah Alice Yoder Egly, 69, wife of Simon Egly, died at 8:45 p.m. Monday in her home at 3122 S. Harrison street in Ft. Wayne, following an illness of one day. She suffered a heart attack Monday morning. She had not been ill p
2 CONC reviously.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Egly was a native of this community. She was born near Linn Grove April 6, 1886, the daughter of Mr. And Mrs. Daniel Yoder. She would have been 70 years of age today. Mrs. Egly was married to Simon Egly Dec. 24, 1904 in Berne
2 CONC  and the couple recently celebrated their golden wedding anniversary. Mrs. Egly had resided in Fort Wayne 21 years and was a member of the First Missionary church in that city.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are her husband, two daughters, Mrs. R. E. Dunlap, Ft. Wayne, and Miss Juanita Egly at home, two grandchildren; two brothers, Noah Yoder, Ft. Wayne, and Joe Yoder, Leo; five sisters, Mrs. Sam Neusbaum, Linn Grove, Mrs. F
2 CONC rank Stuckey, Leo, Mrs. James Maxfield, Leo, Mrs. P. M. Omo, New Carlisle, Mrs. M. O. Klopfenstein, Oneco, Fla, and a sister-in-law, Mrs. David Yoder, Fort Wayne.
2 CONT
2 CONT The body was taken to the D. O. McComb & Sons funeral Home.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be held at 1:00 p.m. Thursday at the funeral home, the Rev. Cornelius Vlot officiating. Burial will be in the M. R. E. cemetery west of Berne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Handwritten-Tuesday April 5, 1955
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Simon Egly
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services for Mrs. Sarah Alice Egly, 69, will be held at 1 p.m. Thursday in the D.O. McComb and Sons Funeral Home, the Rev. Cornelius Vlot officiating. Burial will be in the MRE Cemetery, Berne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Adams County, Indiana Historical Museum"1955Mar-April1958" Scrapbook
