1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Decatur Daily Democrat 
2 CONT Adams County, Indiana 
2 CONT Thursday, June 8, 1922 
2 CONT
2 CONT HARTFORD TOWNSHIP GIRL DIED SUDDENLY FROM HEART TROUBLE MONDAY EVENING 
2 CONT
2 CONT    Funeral services were held at the Missionary church west of Berne this 
2 CONT afternoon at 2 o'clock for Miss Ruth Egly (sic), who died last Monday evening.  
2 CONT The services in the church were preceded by a service at the home at 1 o'clock.  
2 CONT Miss Egley was the oldest child of Mr. and Mrs. Simon Egley, living on the 
2 CONT Abraham Egley farm in Hartford township. 
2 CONT    The cause of the young lady's death was leakage of the heart and pulmonary 
2 CONT tuberculosis.  Although she had been sick for a few months, her condition had 
2 CONT not been considered so serious and her death was rather sudden. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
