1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dorothy Lucile Egly Garner passed this life at 10:09 p.m. on Monday, September 28, 2015 at her home. She was born on July 21, 1923 to Jesse and Ida Schenbeck Egly in Forrest, Illinois. She graduated from Forrest Hi
2 CONC gh School and attended Anderson College in Anderson, Indiana.
2 CONT
2 CONT    She married Harold Franklin “Hal” Garner on November 24, 1946 in Danville, Illinois, and she was always his “Angel.” He survives along with a daughter, Carol (Gary) Paris of Washington, NC, and twin sons, Dennis (Lynn) Garner o
2 CONC f Muncie, IN and David Garner of Peoria, IL. She is also survived by her brothers Glenn Egly of Magonlia, TX and Alan (Pat) Egly of Davenport, IA, and a sister-in-law Patricia (David) Jarvis of Collison, IL. Also surviving are her
2 CONC  grandchildren Caryn (Jeff) Isenhower of Philo, IL, Darin (Dana) Paris of San Marcos, CA, James Garner of Indianapolis, IN, Jeff Garner of Muncie, IN, and her great-granddaughter Abriella Paris of San Marcos, CA.
2 CONT
2 CONT    Dorothy was a member of Community Church of God where she served as Sunday School teacher and on the Church Council, as well as on other committees and boards through the years. She enjoyed music and sang in the church choir as
2 CONC  well as in ensembles. She was a very giving person and always thought of others. Dorothy enjoyed cooking and baking for her family and enjoyed opening her home to others. She worked for many years in the office at Jules Strauss a
2 CONC nd also at the Danville GE Credit Union. She will be truly missed.
2 CONT
2 CONT    She was preceded in death by her parents and six siblings: Arthur Egly, Alice Jochums, Stella Harriet Hewitt, Marian Zerkle, Clara Bounds, and Lois York.
2 CONT
2 CONT    The family wishes to thank all those who have provided care during the past months including the staffs of Dr. Naveed Sadiq, Colonial Manor, Songer Home Care, and Carle Hospice. Thanks also to her church family and many friends
2 CONC  for the calls, cards, visits, and prayers.
2 CONT
2 CONT    Visitation will be at Pape Family Funeral Home, 10 E. Williams Street in Danville on Friday, October 2, 2015 from 4-7pm. Funeral Services will be at 11am on Saturday, October 3, 2015 at Community Church of God, 535 South Bowman
2 CONC  Avenue in Danville, with pastor Jeremy Zerkle and Pastor Corey Stocksdale officiating. Burial will follow at Sunset Memorial Park. Flowers are welcome or memorials can be made to Community Church of God.  Messages and memories ma
2 CONC y be left on our website at www.papefuneral.com, or on the Pape Family Funeral Home Facebook page.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/153068681/dorothy-lucile-garner Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/pro
