1 NOTE {geni:about_me} MAYSVILLE - Mandy E. Hershberger, 72, of 10380 Harrison Road, Apple Creek (Maysville), died Saturday, May 9, 2020 at LifeCare Hospice in Wooster. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born to the late Joseph and Martha (Shetler) Hilty and married Atlee A. Hershberger on November 25, 1971. He died December 30, 2015. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a member of the Old Order Amish Church. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by children, Roy (Anna Marie) Hershberger of Dundee, Robert (Linda Sue) Hershberger of Fredericksburg, Mervin (Miriam) Hershberger and Michael (Ada) Hershberger, both of Apple Creek; 21 grandchildren; one great gra
2 CONC nddaughter; brothers, Daniel Hilty, Henry (Verena) Hilty and Elmer (Esther) Hilty; and sisters, Barbara (John) Graber, Martha (Emanuel) Swartz and Elma (Elmer) Swartz 
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to her parents and husband, she was preceded in death by a sister, Annie (Johnny) Wickey. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held on Tuesday at 9:00 AM at the former Maysville Fabric Store, 10476 Harrison Road, Maysville, with Bishop Martin J. Yoder officiating. Burial will follow in the Hershberger Family Cemetery in Paint Town
2 CONC ship, Wayne County. Friends may call anytime at the Maysville Fabric Store. Spidell Funeral Home in Mount Eaton is handling the arrangements. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The family would like to express their thanks to Home Health Care and LifeCare Hospice for their exceptional care.
