1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jacob Ray Graber was born October 2, 1927, at Allen Co. IN. to Menno and Elizabeth (Eicher) Graber. He passed away at his home on September 12, 2024, at Jamesport, MO. At the age of 96 years 11 months and 10 days. 
2 CONC He was married on February 7, 1949, to Anna Knepp. She preceded him in death on June 25, 1968. They lived in matrimony for 19 years 4 months 18 days. Jacob remarried to Katie (Troyer) Wengerd on February 11, 1969. She preceded him
2 CONC  in death on December 16, 1982. They lived in matrimony for 13 years 10 months and 5 days. Jacob remarried May 27, 1984, to Lydia M. Miller. She survives at the home. They lived in matrimony for 40 years 3 months and 16 days. He w
2 CONC as a member of the Old Order Amish Church; he remained faithful to the end.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He leaves to mourn 6 sons and 7 daughters. Ruth (Crist) Mast, Townville, PA. Rosie (Elvan) Schrock, Jamesport, MO. Sara (Eli) Mast, Meadville, PA. Dorothy (Atlee) Miller, Orrville, OH. Dave (Alma) Graber, Sugarcreek, OH. Jacob Jr.
2 CONC  (Mary) Graber, Jamesport, MO. John (Karen) Graber, Millersburg, OH. Esther (JR) Wengerd, Gambier, OH. Daughter-in-law, Rosie (Yoder) Graber, Jamesport, MO. Paul (Ruth Ann) Graber, Loganville, WI. Martha (Roy) Hershberger, Bethleh
2 CONC am, OH. Syl (Christina) Graber, Jamesport, MO. Kathryn (Dave) Myers, Holmesville, OH. Rueben (Laura) Graber, Sugarcreek, OH. Two step-children, Edna (Albert) Yoder, Millersburg, OH. David (Martha) Wengerd, Baltic, OH.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He also leaves 94 grandchildren, 15 step-grandchildren, 273 great-grandchildren, 18 step-great grandchildren, 15 great-great grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by son, Phillip, 6 grandchildren, 3 great-grandchildren. Father, Mother, brothers, Melvin and Sylvan and sisters, Elizabeth, Ada and Ruth.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The family wishes to thank everyone for their prayers and acts of kindness during this time of sorrow.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held at 9:00 AM, Monday, September 16, 2024, at the Atlee Miller Residence, 3522 TR 371 Sugarcreek, OH. Burial will follow at Miller Cemetery in Sugarcreek, Ohio. Friends may call at the Atlee Miller resid
2 CONC ence from 2:00-4:00 and 5:30-8:00 PM on Sunday. A funeral service will be held at 9:00 AM, Saturday, September 14, 2024, at the Abe Kurtz Residence in Jamesport, Missouri prior to being transported to Ohio for services and burial.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Miller Funeral Care -Walnut Creek, OH 330-893-2273
