1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ELIZABETH BETTY JEAN WAGLER, 79, died on Monday July 6, 2009, at Community Memorial Hospital, Hicksville. Born Feb. 2, 1930, in Grabill, she was the daughter of Menno and Elizabeth (Eicher) Graber. She married Wilm
2 CONC er Wagler in 1951. She was a member of Hicksville Mennonite Church; an avid gardener; and loved sewing and reading. She is survived by six sons, Daniel (Donna) of Auburn, William (Linda) Hicksville, Ohio, Menno (Ada) of Hudson, In
2 CONC d., Joe (Kathy) of Sarasota, Fla., James (Abagail) of Fremont, and Michael (Tanya) of Hudson; three daughters, Mary (Kenny) Crites of Hicksville, Ohio, Julia (Kenny) Wallace of Nashville, Tenn. and Hannah (Dwayne) Weaver of Whitti
2 CONC er, N.C.; 19 grandchildren; 12 great-grandchildren; a sister, Ada Troyer of Orrville, Ohio; and a brother, Jacob Ray Graber of Jamesport, Mo. She was preceded in death by her husband in 2006; a son, Wilmer Jr.; a daughter, Elizabe
2 CONC th; a sister, Ruth Ilene; and two brothers, Melvin and infant, Sylvan Leon. Funeral service is 10 a.m. Friday at Hicksville Mennonite Church. Visitation is from 5 to 8 p.m. Wednesday and from 3 to 5 and 6 to 8 p.m. Thursday at the
2 CONC  Hicksville Mennonite Church Gymnasium. Burial in Lost Creek Cemetery, Farmer Township, Ohio. Memorials may be made to Hicksville Mennonite Church Building Fund. Condolences may be shared at www.smithbrownfuneralhome.com
