1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ORRVILLE -- Ada Marie Troyer, 84, 433 N. Swinehart Road, Orrville, passed away Wednesday, Oct. 19, 2016, at her home. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born in Allen County, Ind., on June 12, 1932, to the late Menno and Elizabeth (Eicher) Graber and married John L. Troyer on Jan. 17, 1957. He died April 20, 2005. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a member of the Old Order Amish Church. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are children, Ruth (Alvin) Yoder of Apple Creek, Jake (Naomi) Troyer of Bremen, Ind., Marvin (Vera) Troyer of the home, Becky (Atlee) Troyer of Orrville, Neal (Arie) Troyer of Fredericksburg, Elizabeth (Delon) Troyer of 
2 CONC Sugarcreek, Mary (Harry) Wagler of Apple Creek, Barbara (Rodger) Wash of Tulsa, Okla., Esther (Paul) Troyer of Apple Creek, Martha (Levi) Miller of Brinkhaven, John Jr. Troyer of the home, Rosanna (Andy) Kauffman of Apple Creek, A
2 CONC da (Robert) Keim of Fredericksburg, Vernon Troyer and Edna Troyer, both of the home, and Susan (Edward) Yoder of Orrville; 77 grandchildren; 32 great-grandchildren; a brother, Jake (Lydia) Graber of Jamesport, Mo.; and a sister-in
2 CONC -law, Wilma Eash of Indiana. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to her husband, she was preceded in death by her parents; two brothers; two sisters; a grandson, Robbie; and an infant grandson. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be Friday at 9:30 a.m. at the Atlee Troyer residence, 500 N. Carr Road, Orrville, with Bishop Mose Miller officiating. Burial will be in the Erb Cemetery, East Union Township. Friends may call anytime at the 
2 CONC Atlee Troyer residence. Spidell Funeral Home in Mount Eaton is handling arrangements. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The family would like to thank the staff of LifeCare Hospice for their kind and loving care.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ada Marie Troyer, 84, 433 N. Swinehart Road, Orrville, passed away Wednesday, Oct. 19, 2016, at her home.
2 CONT
