1 NOTE {geni:about_me} David Miller, 82 years, 11 months, and 25 days old, of New Haven, Indiana, a retired farmer & blacksmith, died at 11:45 p.m. on October 27, 1969, at Parkview Memorial Hospital, where he was a patient for one day, h
2 CONC is death followed a long illness.  He was born in Springfield township on November 2, 1886 to parents: Jacob and Catherine "Katie" (Stoll) Miller.
2 CONT David married on December 11, 1910 to Lucy Delagrange. He resided in the Harlan area his entire life. He was member of the Old Order Amish Church. Surviving sons; Victor (Rosa Ann Delagrange) Miller of Leo, Indiana, Joseph (Margar
2 CONC et) Miller of New Haven, Indiana; William (Amanda) Miller of New Haven, Indiana, Jacob (Anna Rebecca) Miller of Grabill, Indiana, David (Leah) Miller, Jr of Grabill, Indiana.
2 CONT Surviving daughters: Rosa Schmucker of New Haven, Indiana; Ida (Noah) Schmucker of Woodburn, Indiana, Lillie (Joseph) Graber of Grabill, Indiana, Lucy (Emanuel D) Graber of New Haven, Indiana.
2 CONT 53 grandchildren & 45 great-grandchildren.
2 CONT David was preceded in death by wife: Lucy (Delagrange) Miller who died December 19, 1938, and son, John (Rosa) Miller who December 26, 1966.
2 CONT Funeral service will be 9:30 am Thursday October 30, 1969 at the residence, Samuel J Graber officiating. Burial will be in Amish Cemetery.
2 CONT Friends may call at the residence. Arrangements by the Oetting Funeral Home, Harlan, Indiana.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/76221183/david_miller Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy
