1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lucy Miller Graber was born August 7, 1930, Allen County, Indiana, and died April 8, 2017, Allen County, Indiana
2 CONT Her parents were David Miller and Lucy DeLaGrange
2 CONT she married on May 4, 1950 to Emanuel Jacob Graber
2 CONT They had no children~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~LUCY GRABER ObituaryLUCY GRABER, 86, passed away Saturday, April 8, 2017 at her home in New Haven. She was a native and lifetime r
2 CONC esident of New Haven and Allen Co. Indiana. Lucy was the daughter of the late David and Lucy Miller. She was a homemaker and loving wife and aunt. Lucy was a member of the Old Order Amish Church. Surviving are her nephew and careg
2 CONC iver, Sam and Clara Mae Graber of New Haven, Ind.; sisters-in-law, Ida Marie Graber, Leah Miller, Mary Ann Graber, Elizabeth Graber; brother-in -aw Martin and sister-in-law Rebecca Brandenberger; brother-in-law Jacob and sister-in
2 CONC -law Catherine Brandenberger; and many nieces and nephews. Lucy was preceded in death by husband, Emanuel Graber; sisters, Ida Schmucker, Rosa Schmucker, Lillie Graber; brothers, John Miller, Victor Miller, Jacob Miller, Joseph Mi
2 CONC ller, William Miller and David Miller. Service is 9 a.m. Tuesday, April 11, 2017 at the Graber family home, 15616 Ehle Rd., New Haven (IN 46774). Bishop Daniel Graber officiating. Calling will begin Sunday April 9, 2017 at the hom
2 CONC e until the day of service. Burial in Milan Center Amish Cemetery, New Haven, Ind. Arrangements by D.O McComb & Sons Lakeside Park Funeral Home, 1140 Lake Ave, Fort Wayne, Ind.Published by Fort Wayne Newspapers on Apr. 10, 2017.* 
