1 NOTE {geni:about_me} LOUIS LEE LENGACHER, 78, of Grabill, died peacefully Thursday, June 8, 2006, at Visiting Nurse & Hospice Home, Fort Wayne. Born May 1, 1928, in Allen County, he was the son of the late Amos and Emma (Dela-grange) L
2 CONC en-gacher. He was a commercial contractor for over 50 years building many of the city's landmark buildings, including numerous churches, hotels, renovating city park buildings, Midtown Crossing, Glenbrook Square and participated i
2 CONC n the building of the Grand Wayne Center and the City Parking Garage to name a few. He was a member of the Grabill Missionary Church serving as a Deacon and Elder in the past. He loved his family and the Lord and served Him faithf
2 CONC ully. He enjoyed the teaching and fellowship of the Bridgebuilders Sunday School class he attended. He is survived by his wife of 57 years, Margueriette (Weirich) Lengacher; two sons, Ralph (wife, Lee) Lengacher of Fort Wayne and 
2 CONC Reynold (wife, Kim) Lengacher of Orlando, Fla.; two daughters, Glenda (husband, Stan) Whittern of Grabill and Mona (husband, Marlin) Steury of Leo; nine grandchildren, Cindi (husband, Tom) DeSomer of Oswego N.Y., Matt Whittern of 
2 CONC Fort Wayne, Ashley (husband, Chris) Parent of Fort Wayne, Casey (wife, Rebecca) Lengacher of Lexington, Ky., Kyle Steury, Kayla Steury and Kortney Steury, all of Leo, Amber Lengacher and Riley Lengacher, both of Orlando, Fla.; thr
2 CONC ee great-grandchildren, Alexa, Caleb and Patrick. He was preceded in death by one brother, Mervin Lengacher.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/87258398/louis_lee_lengacher Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.
