2 CONT
2 CONT     Obit - Gospel Herald:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Histand.-Samuel Swartz Histand, son of Samuel and Rebecca Overholt Histan d, was born April 9, 1871, in Doylestown Twp., Pa.; passed to his etern al reward March 21, 1944; aged almost 73 years. On Oct. 26, 1895, he was m arrie
2 CONC d to Susie Landis who survives him together with 13 children: Samuel Jr., Doylestown, Pa.; Elizabeth, wife of James Gross, Harrisonburg, Va .: Daniel, Doylestown; Rebecca, wife of J. Silas Graybill, Souderton, Pa .; Howard, New Ho
2 CONC pe, Pa.; Mary, wife of David Alderfer, Scottdale, Pa.; Ru th, wife of John Mosemann, Lancaster, Pa.; Laura, Akron, Pa.; Susie at home; William, Doylestown; Sara, wife of Vernon Schmidt, Paraguay, S.A.; David, Tinicum, Pa.; James, 
2 CONC Denbigh, Va. Two sons and one daughter, Isaac, Abram, and Florence preceded him in death. He is also survived by 28 grandchi ldren and 4 sisters. His only brother, Bishop A. O. Histand, preceded h im in death by only 7 months. Dea
2 CONC th was caused by a heart aliment after se veral years of failing health. He was a devout Christian and a kind husband and father. Services were conducted at the Doylestown Mennonite Chur ch by Joseph Gross, J. C. Clemens, and J. S
2 CONC ilas Graybill. The latter, a so n-in-law, assisted by the request of the deceased. Interment was made in t he adjoining cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=18659339
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT A Brief History of Jacob Wismer and a Complete Genealogical Family Register With Biographies of His Descendants from the Earliest Available Records to the Present Time By A J Fretz, Eli Wismer 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://books.google.com/books?id=nwBgAAAAMAAJ 
2 CONT
2 CONT Page xiii, 7, 8, 10, 11
2 CONT
2 CONT I. Jacob Wismer, (...) was born in Germany about 1684, and died in Bedminster Township, Bucks Co., Pa., Feb. 4, 1787 in his one hundred and third year. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (...) 
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Jacob and Nanny Wismer, as near in the order of birth as could be placed were: ---Jacob, Mary, Elizabeth, Joseph, Henry, Mark, Daniel, John, Christian, Nanny, Abraham.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Jacob Wismer,* bn. in Bucks Co., Pa., about 1721. Mrd. Margaret ---. The dates of death of himself and wife are not known. He received his portion of his father's estate in 1783. Lived in Plumstead Twp. at what is known as the
2 CONC  burnt mill, where he followed the occupation of miller. Children: Abraham, Isaac, Anna, Mary, Elizabeth, Jacob, Mary, Barbara, Hannah, Margaret.
2 CONT
2 CONT III. Rev. Abraham Wismer, bn. in Bucks Co., Aug. 21, 1746. Mrd. ---. He was familiarly known as Abraham Wismer, the "long-beard." Children: Barbara, Margaret, Elizabeth, Hannah, Magdalena.
2 CONT
2 CONT IV. Margaret Wismer, bn.—. Mrd. Abraham Overholt.—. Children: Jacob, Abraham, Isaac, Henry.
2 CONT
2 CONT V. Abraham Overholt, bn.—. Mrd. Magdalena Gross,—. Children: Joseph, Mary, Rebecca, Henry, Susanna, Isaac, Abraham.
2 CONT
2 CONT VI. Rebecca Overholt, bn. Aug. 18, 1836. Mrd. Samuel Histand, Dec. 17, 1864. P. O., Doylestown, Pa. Farmer. Menn. Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Samuel S. Histand, bn. Apr. 9,1871.
