1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/90128600/abraham-landis-histand
2 CONT
2 CONT Gospel Herald Vol 29 #26; 24 Sep 1936 pp 558-9
2 CONT
2 CONT Histand-Abram L., son of Samuel and Susie (Landis) Histand, was born Oct. 15, 1899; died at his home near Doylestown, Pa., Sept. 2, 1936; aged 36 y. 10 m. 17 d. He was preceded in death by his daughter (Hannah), 1 brother (Isaac),
2 CONC  and 1 sister (Florence). He was united in marriage to Fannie Good of East Petersburg, Pa., Aug. 21, 1924. To this union were born 3 children. Surviving him are his widow, 1 son (Ernest), 1 daughter (Rhoda), his father and mother,
2 CONC  7 sisters, and 6 brothers. In his infancy he with his parents moved to the farm on which he lived practically all his life. In May his health began to fail. Doctors were at a loss to know the reason for it, and finally found his 
2 CONC liver was enlarged; the rarest type of its kind. He never suffered pain but got weaker until Sept. 2, at 3 P. M., he peacefully passed away. He left us with the assurance that he was saved and was anxiously awaiting the Lord to co
2 CONC me and take him home. Being so young, he was much needed yet; but we resign to God's will. He was a kind and loving husband and father, of a devoted and peaceful disposition. He will be missed in the home, Church, community and bu
2 CONC siness. A large concourse of friends gathered to pay their last tribute of respect to one who was much loved.
