1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/90127050/howard-l_-histand
2 CONT
2 CONT Morning Call (Allentown, PA), 2 Aug 1990
2 CONT
2 CONT Howard L. Histand, 85, of the Rockhill Mennonite Community, Sellersville, died Tuesday in his home. He was the husband of the late Alma (Kulp) Histand.
2 CONT
2 CONT He operated a retail sales and service business in Hatboro, Montgomery County, selling Culligan water conditioning products. He was also a hosiery knitter in Doylestown and Lambertville, N.J., for several years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Doylestown, he was a son of the late Samuel S. and Susan (Overholt) Histand.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a member of Doylestown Mennonite Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors: Daughter, Lois N. Gilbert of Hagerstown, Md.; brothers, William of Fountainville, Bucks County, David of Telford and James of Denbigh, Va.; sisters, Elizabeth Gross, Mary Alderfer and Laura, all of Harrisonburg, Va., Ru
2 CONC th Mosemann of Goshen, Ind., and Rebecca Graybill of Sellersville; four grandchildren and one great-grandson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arrangements, Anders-Detweiler Funeral Home, Souderton.
