2 CONT Histand, Susie L., daughter of the late Samuel S. and Susie Landis Histand, was born April 14, 1910, at Doylestown, Pa.; died May 29, 1954, in a sister's home at Harrisonburg, Va.; aged 44 y. 1 m. 15 d. She was a faithful member o
2 CONC f the Doylestown Mennonite Church since childhood and was possessed of a strong faith and a quiet but persuasive Christian spirit, and constantly sought the will of God for her life. She sacrificed many personal privileges and adv
2 CONC antages for the sake of others, caring faithfully for her parents while they lived and then for other members of her family. For several years she was on the kitchen staff at Goshen College. All who knew her were helped by her Chr
2 CONC istian attitudes and testimony, and feel a loss in her passing, which was caused by cancer. 
