2 CONT
2 CONT Henry L. Ruth‚ a resident of the Souderton Mennonite Homes‚ died at the home of John and Roma Ruth in Lower Salford Twp.‚ Feb. 26‚ 2006. In the previous month‚ his family had celebrated his 101st birthday at his Souderton residenc
2 CONC e.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born Jan. 7‚ 1905 on a farm on New Galena Road in New Britain Twp.‚ Henry was the fifth of seven children of Allen R. and Sallie (Landis) Ruth. After attending the neighboring former Fairview Elementary School and two years at hig
2 CONC h schools in Newville and Chalfont‚ he worked at home and on the farms of Horace Ruth in New Britain‚ Menno Souder of near Elroy‚ and his older brother‚ Ervin Ruth‚ of near Hatfield.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Susan A. Landis of Lower Salford‚ March 20‚ 1929‚ and moved to her parents' farm along the Branch Creek‚ where he was a hired man until 1941. He then farmed for himself until the mid 1970s‚ renting the farm from his bro
2 CONC ther-in-law‚ Abram A. Landis.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1931‚ they were founding members of the Finland Mennonite congregation‚ where Henry served as Sunday school secretary and teacher and retained lifelong membership.
2 CONT
2 CONT As a young farmer‚ Henry cultivated interests in photography and astronomy‚ developing his own photographs and building his own six-inch reflecting telescope. After concluding dairying‚ he raised beef cattle and worked as an order
2 CONC ly at Grand View Hospital for 14 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1987 the Ruths moved to the Souderton Mennonite Homes‚ where they celebrated their 75th wedding anniversary‚ March 29‚ 2004. Susan died Feb. 11‚ 2005‚ at the age of 95. Both husband and wife lived longer than any of their paren
2 CONC ts or siblings.
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorial services were held on March 2 in the chapel of the Souderton Mennonite Homes, followed by interment in the cemetery of Finland Mennonite Church in Pennsburg.
