1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Norman R. Landis: Newspaper Obituary and Death Notice Intelligencer, The (Doylestown, PA) - March 30, 2011 Deceased Name: Norman R. Landis Norman R. Landis of Souderton, formerly of Perkasie, entered into rest on S
2 CONC unday, March 27, 2011 at Souderton Mennonite Homes. He was 96. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the husband of the late Mary (Rice) Landis. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Normal was born in New Britain Township to the late Samuel and Anna (Rosenberger) Landis. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Norman worked as a clerk for the former Gross Grocery in Souderton. He had a bakery route for the former Fly's Bakery in the Harleysville area. Norman was employed as a clerk for Landis Supermarket in Telford until his retirement.
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a member of the Mennonite Heritage Center in Harleysville. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Norman wrote the history of Salem Mennonite Church and the Landis family history. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He enjoyed genealogy, history, writing, reading and gardening. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Norman was a member of Salem Mennonite Church of Quakertown, where he was a former Sunday school teacher and was very active in the church. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by his daughter, Sara Davis and her husband, Ron, of Reading, Pa.; two grandchildren and five great-grandchildren. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by his first wife, Emma Landis; his two brothers, Paul and Raymond Landis; and his sister, Mary Fly. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held at 11 a.m. Thursday, March 31 at Souderton Mennonite Homes, 207 W. Summit Street, Souderton, where friends may meet with the family from 10 to 11 a.m. Burial will take place at Deep Run Mennonite Ceme
2 CONC tery East. 
