1 NOTE {geni:about_me} FREDERICKSBURG Eli R. Troyer, 92, 6178 Harrison Road, died Friday, June 17, 2005, at his residence after a period of declining health. Services will be Monday at 9 a.m. at the residence, with Bishop John Yoder offi
2 CONC ciating. Burial will be at Troyer Cemetery, Salt Creek Township, Wayne County. Friends may call anytime at the residence. Arrangements are being handled by Murray Funeral Home in Fredericksburg. He was born July 31, 1912, in Milan
2 CONC d, Mich., to Rudy C. and Amanda (Otto) Troyer and married Amanda Hershberger on Dec. 27, 1938. She died Nov. 17, 1989. He had made his home in Wayne County most of his life and was a member of the Old Order Amish. Surviving are ch
2 CONC ildren, Fannie (Henry S.) Miller and Melvin (Lizzie) Troyer, both of Fredericksburg, Milton (Fannie) Troyer of Shreve, Susie (Crist) Yoder, Sadie (Andy) Schlabach and Atlee (Katie) Troyer, all of Millersburg, Esther (Lester) Chupp
2 CONC , Ada (Joe) Miller and Jacob (Katie) Troyer, all of Holmesville, Eli Jr. (Kathy) Troyer of Waynesville, N.C., and Lizzie (Levi) Wengerd of the home; 57 grandchildren; 87 great-grandchildren; and brothers, Jacob R. and Noah R. Troy
2 CONC er, both of Fredericksburg, Milton R. and Menno R. Troyer, both of Apple Creek and Dan R. Troyer of Holmesville. In addition to his wife, an infant son, two granddaughters, two brothers and four sisters died previously.
