1 NOTE {geni:about_me} MILLERSBURG -- Menno R. Troyer, 83, 7655 State Route 241, Millersburg, formerly of Maysville, died Saturday, Nov. 17, 2007, at 12:15 p.m. at the home of his son, Dan M. Troyer, with whom he had resided. His death f
2 CONC ollowed a period of declining health.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be Tuesday, Nov. 20, at 9 a.m. at the Jacob Troyer Jr. residence, 10133 Harrison Road, Apple Creek (west of Maysville) with Bishop Leroy A. Keim officiating. Burial will be in Yoder Cemetery, Salt Creek Township, Way
2 CONC ne County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Friends may call anytime at the Dan M. Troyer residence, 7655 State Route 241, Millersburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spidell Funeral Home in Mount Eaton is handling arrangements.
2 CONT
2 CONT Menno was born March 11, 1924, in Wayne County to the late Rudy C. and Amanda (Otto) Troyer and married Mattie J. Weaver on Dec. 7, 1944. She died April 13, 1986. On June 16, 1987, he married Iva Troyer (daughter of Eli D. and Emm
2 CONC a (Miller) Troyer). She survives.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had lived all of his life in this area and was a member of the Old Order Amish Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving in addition to his wife are sons, Dan M. (Anna) Troyer of the home, Abe M.R. (Emma) Troyer of Fredericksburg and Jacob M. (Amanda) Troyer of Howard; daughters, Fannie, Lizzie and Amanda Troyer, all of Apple Creek (Maysvi
2 CONC lle); 30 grandchildren; 89 great-grandchildren; brothers, Dan R. (Anna) Troyer of Holmesville and Noah R. (Nancy) Troyer of Fredericksburg; and a sister-in-law, Emma (Crist) Troyer of Apple Creek.
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to his first wife, he was preceded in death by brothers, Jonas, Eli, Crist, Milton and Jacob, and sisters, Annie, Lydia, Katie and Lizzie.
