1 BURI
2 PLAC Sand Flat Cemetery, Tyler,															Smith County,															Texas,																USA
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 14 FEB 1925
2 PLAC Midland, Midland County, Texas, USA
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 25 JUN 2013
2 PLAC Tyler, Smith County, Texas, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Funeral services for Mr. Floyd Helmuth age 88 of Tyler are scheduled for 2:00 PM, Friday- June 28, 2013 in the chapel of Caudle-Rutledge Funeral Home in Lindale with burial to follow in the Sand Flat Cemetery with 
2 CONC Pastor Randy Edwards officiating. Mr. Helmuth died Tuesday June 25, 2013 in a Tyler hospital, he was born February 14, 1925 in Midland, Michigan and was formerly of Illinois and Florida before moving to Tyler in 1967. Mr. Helmuth 
2 CONC served in the United States Navy during World War II was a member of the Crossbrand Cowboy Church in Tyler. He had worked as a rancher and for Southland Distribution and Tyler Foam Company. He was preceded in death by 10 brothers 
2 CONC and sisters and by a granddaughter, Pamala G. Scott in June of 2003. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Helmuth is survived by wife, Dorothy Helmuth of Tyler; 3 Daughters and 2 Sons-in-law; Margaret Sperry of Murchison, Donna and Bobby Van Ness of Tyler and Carol & Larry Brock of Gilmer, a Son and Daughter-in-law; James T. and M
2 CONC argaret H. Helmuth of Tyler. Sister; Fran Lengacher of Alburn, Indiana, a Brother-in-law; Enos J. Helmuth of Arthur, Indiana and by 8 Grandchildren, 11 Great-Grandchildren, 8 Great Great-Grandchildren, and Numerous Nieces and Neph
2 CONC ews. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pallbearers will be Kyle Casey, Bobby Van Ness, Jr., Ret. Col. Stan Murrell, Joe Cooper, Joe Vickery, and Lawrence Cannon. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Published in Tyler Morning Telegraph on June 27, 2013* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/112954439/floyd_menno_helmuth Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 3 2024,
2 CONC  1:25:06 UTC''
