1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Amanda Funk, 95, of Millersburg, died at 1:38 pm, on Sunday, March 5, at her residence.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born on November 1, 1921, in Hutchinson, KS, to Noah and Rosa (Schrock) Nisly. On June 15, 1952 in Hutchinson, KS she married Walter Funk; he died November 30, 1996.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving is a son, Harry (Margie) Funk of New Carlisle; two daughters, Marie (Ben) Whirledge and Betty Funk both of Millersburg; five grandchildren, two step grandchildren, four great grandchildren, three step great grandchildren
2 CONC ; two sisters, Rebecca (Albert) Miller and Ella Nisly both of Partridge, KS; two brothers, Amos (Anne) Nisly of Hutchinson, KS and Moses (Mary) Nisly of Shreve, OH; a sister-in-law, Velma Plank of Goshen.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by her husband, parents, son, Ruben Funk, grandson, Jason Funk, three brothers, Will, Abraham and Joe Nisly, two sisters, Lydia Yoder and Anna Raber.
2 CONT
2 CONT Amanda was a member of Clinton Brick Mennonite Church, of Millersburg. She was a volunteer at the World Missionary Press and a willing participant in numerous church activities. She was a lifelong example of what a Godly Christian
2 CONC  woman could be, and also a wonderful, loving and energetic wife, mother, sister, aunt, grandmother and great-grandmother.
2 CONT
2 CONT Visitation will be from 5:00 - 8:00 pm on Tuesday March 7, at Miller-Stewart Funeral Home, 1003 South Main Street Middlebury.
2 CONT
2 CONT There will also be one hour of visitation prior to the 10:30 am funeral service on Wednesday March 8, at Clinton Brick Mennonite Church, Goshen. Services will be conducted by Pastor David Hathaway.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial will be in Clinton Brick Cemetery, Goshen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorials may be given to World Missionary Press or Clinton Brick Mennonite Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/177043568/amanda-funk
2 CONT
