1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Barbara E. Weaver, 86, of Goshen, formerly of Middlebury, died at 1:20 pm, on Wednesday, January 21, at Greencroft Health Care Center, Goshen. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born on November 12, 1928, in Buchanan County, IA, to David and Mattie (Yoder) Schrock. On February 27, 1949 in Wakarusa she married Lowell E. Weaver; he died April 12, 2013. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are two sons, Tom (Barbara) Weaver of Goshen, Steve (Susan) Weaver of Salt Lake City, UT; two daughters, Rebecca (Gary) Cline of Swoope, VA, Patricia Weaver of CA; nine grandchildren, five great- grandchildren; sister, S
2 CONC ue Kurtz of Goshen; three brothers, Edward Schrock of Goshen, Bob Schrock of Mishawaka, David Schrock of Indianapolis. She is also survived by her faithful companion Coco. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by her husband, parents, brother, Alvin Schrock, three sisters, Elizabeth Beck, Alma Bontrager and Mary Yoder. Barbara was a charter member of Bonneyville Mennonite Church where she was very faithful in a
2 CONC ttending. She was a homemaker, had been a telephone operator in Elkhart and had been a secretary with her husband for their different woodworking businesses. She loved flowers, enjoyed gardening, watching birds and riding motorcyc
2 CONC le with her husband. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Visitation will begin at 3:00 pm followed by a memorial service at 4:00 on Saturday January 24, at Bonneyville Mennonite Church, Bristol. Services will be conducted by Pastor Marcella Hershberger. The family will have a private bu
2 CONC rial service at Grace Lawn Cemetery prior to the memorial service.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/141658459/barbara-e_-weaver Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''
