1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mary L. Yoder, 74, passed away Saturday, May 10, at Elkhart General Hospital.  She was born in 1939, in Hutchinson, Kan., to David and Mattie (Yoder) Schrock.  On July 25, 1959, she married Ray Yoder in Wakarusa.  
2 CONC She is survived by two children, Laurie (Tim) Mast of ElDorado, Ark. and Len A. (Beverly) Yoder of White Pigeon, Mich.; three siblings, Edward Schrock, Susan Kurtz and Barbara Weaver all of Goshen; brother-in-law Gene Bontreger of
2 CONC  LaGrange; half-brothers David Schrock of Indianapolis and Robert Schrock of South Bend ; two grandchildren, Audrey (Daniel) Amsler of Rensselaer and Robyn (Daniel) Stinson of Alexanderia; and five great-grandchildren.  She was pr
2 CONC eceded in death by her parents and three siblings, Alvin Schrock, Elizabeth Beck and Alma Bontreger.  She loved the Lord and her family. 
2 CONT
