1 NOTE {geni:about_me} LaGrange — Alma Bontreger, 83, died Wednesday at Miller’s Merry Manor in LaGrange.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs Bontreger was born on Jan 10, 1931 in Hutchinson, Kan, to Dave and Mattie (Yoder) Schrock. She had lived for many years in LaGrange County, moving to the area from Elkhart County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs Bontreger was a homemaker and had also worked as a bookkeeper for more than 30 years at the Wolcottville Grain Elevator and had also worked at Starcraft in Topeka. She was a member of the Emma Mennonite Church in Emma.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Oct 16, 1954 in Wakarusa, she married Gene Bontreger. He survives in LaGrange. Also surviving are three sons and daughters-in-law, Tim (Jean) Bontreger of White Pigeon, Mich, Ron (Joann) Bontreger of LaGrange, and Rick and Jenn
2 CONC y Bontreger of Goshen; eight grandchildren; 15 great-grandchildren; three sisters, Sue Kurtz of Goshen, Barbara Weaver of Goshen, and Mary Yoder of Middlebury; and a brother, Edward Schrock of Goshen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her parents; a sister, Elizabeth Beck; and a brother, Alvin Schrock preceded her in death.
2 CONT
2 CONT A memorial service will be held at Emma Mennonite Church Saturday at 10 am with the Rev. Gene Hartman officiating. Memorials may be made to Emma Mennonite Church. Frurip-May Funeral Home in LaGrange, IN is assisting the family wit
2 CONC h arrangements..
2 CONT
2 CONT Goshen News 5 February 2014* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/184580908/alma-bontreger Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 7 2020, 22:35:27 UTC''
