1 NOTE {geni:about_me} SUGARCREEK -- Mattie L. Mast, 85, State Route 39, Sugarcreek, died Friday, March 29, 2013, at her home.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born Oct. 3, 1927, in Iowa to the late Levi C. and Sarah (Schrock) Miller, and married Ora A. Mast on Aug. 29, 1950. He died in 1983.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a homemaker and a member of Living Water Fellowship Church in Sugarcreek.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are children Marlowe (Ellen) Mast of Macon, Miss., Sarah Ann (Lloyd) Hostetler of Goshen, Ind., Dwight (Mabel) Mast of Sugarcreek, Leroy (Cheryl) Mast of Sarasota, Fla., Duane (Katie) Mast of Macon, Miss., Juanita Ruth (
2 CONC Russel) Horst of Dalton, Lynn (Esther) Mast of Kimbolton, and Rita Fay (Gerald) Gingrich of Sioux Falls, S.D.; 37 grandchildren; 25 great-grandchildren; brothers and sisters, Chris Miller of Annabelle, Mo., Harvey Miller of Goshen
2 CONC , Ind., Levi Miller of Reading, Iowa, Barbara Miller of Topeka, Ind., and Sadie Elliott of Columbia, Mo.
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to her husband, she was preceded in death by a grandson; a great-granddaughter; her parents; a brother, Joseph; and sisters Polly, Edna and Susie.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be Monday, April 1, at 10 a.m. at Maranatha Fellowship Church in Sugarcreek, with pastor James B. Mullet officiating. Burial will be in Chester Mennonite Church Cemetery in Wooster.
2 CONT
2 CONT Friends may call Sunday from 2-4 and 6-8 p.m. at Maranatha Fellowship Church. Arrangements are being handled by Smith-Varns Funeral Home in Sugarcreek.
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorials may be made to FIRE International, P.O. Box 5306, Concord, N.C. 28027, and in the memo line write Tony and Kristi Gingrich.
