1 NAME Jonas D. /Yoder/ Sr.
2 GIVN Jonas D.
2 SURN Yoder
2 NSFX Sr.
2 _MARNM Yoder
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Borkholder Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Bremen
3 STAE Indiana
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 15 JAN 1831
2 ADDR
3 CITY Tuscarawas
3 STAE Ohio
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 25 MAY 1924
2 ADDR
3 STAE Indiana
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [  https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/143554606/jonas-yoder]    
2 CONT
2 CONT The following bio is from a typed four page document and is entered here as it was typed, probably from Jonas's own words, either written or spoken, on his 90th birthday:
2 CONT
2 CONT I am a son of a family of fourteen children, eight sons and six daughters, and I am the only one living. My father's name was Daniel Yoder. He had two brother's, Steven and Christian. Steven lived on a farm near where Sugarcreek, 
2 CONC Ohio is now located, and Christian lived about three miles south of Canton, Ohio. My birthplace was one mile north of Shanesville, Ohio.
2 CONT
2 CONT My parents and grandparents together moved from Somerset County, Pennsylvania to Tuscarawas County, Ohio in the year 1812. My grandfather's name was (John) Hans Yoder, and Grandmother's name was Stutzman before her marriage. Grand
2 CONC father came from Switzerland in his youth, if I am informed right.
2 CONT
2 CONT My mother's name (maiden) was also Barbara Yoder, a daughter of (John) Hannes Yoder, and her mother's maiden name was Rickenbach, being my grandmother. Grandfather Yoder died when my mother was a young girl, and Grandmother was ma
2 CONC rried again to a widower, Michael Troyer. My mother had three half brothers and one half-sister, who was married to David Lantz. They had no children. I well remember of seeing these grandparents, and all these folks came from the
2 CONC  Glades, Somerset County, Pennsylvania, to Ohio.
2 CONT
2 CONT I left Ohio in October, 1852 and came to Marshall County, Indiana, this being sixty-eight years ago in 1920, and below I give a few more facts concerning my family.
2 CONT
2 CONT I was born in Tuscarawas County, Ohio January 15, 1831, and was married to Magdalena Gary, December 24, 1854 in La Grande County, Indiana. To this union were born three children. First, an infant son, born dead in October 1855. Se
2 CONC cond, Susana Yoder, born October 27, 1856. Third, William Yoder, born August 13, 1858. Their mother died August 19, 1858.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married the second time to Anna Kaufman of Elkhart County, Indiana, November 24, 1861, and to this union were born five children. Sarah, born November 15, 1863. Levi, born December 11, 1865. Manasses, born November 25, 1869, John 
2 CONC J. Yoder, born December 12, 1871, and Jonas J. Yoder, born December 21st, 1873. Levi Yoder died August 2, 1866.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Yoder married Moses Guengerich, and they had one son. Mother and child both died March 1884.
2 CONT
2 CONT Manasses Yoder married Lillian Kaufman, widow of Jesse Kaufman, her maiden name being Becknell. To this union were born three sons and one daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT John J. Yoder married Elizabeth Troyer, and to this union were born six children, three sons and three daughters. One son and one daughter died.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonas J. Yoder was married to Magalena Hochstetler, and to them were born seven children, four sons and three daughters. Their first born child died in infancy.
2 CONT
2 CONT John J. Yoder's daughter, Sarah, is married to Levi Schrock, and to them is born one daughter to date.
2 CONT
2 CONT Susanna Yoder married Daniel S. Mullet, of Holmes County, Ohio, and to them were born sixteen children, five sons and eleven daughters. Six died in infancy. Sarah married Gideon Chupp, and they have no children. Mary married Henry
2 CONC  C. Hochsteter, and to them are born three sons and four daughters. Benedict D. Mullet married Fannie Miller, of Arthur, Illinois, and to them are born five sons, one daughter. One son died in infancy. Mattie married Issac D. Yode
2 CONC r, and they have five children, three sons and two daughters. Susan married Henry Graber, of North Dakota, and to them is born one son. Tona married Manasses S. Yoder and to them are born three children, two sons and one daughter.
2 CONC  Daniel Mullet, Jr. married Celesta Hochetetler, and to them are born one son and one daughter. Amanda and Emma are single to this date - January 15, 1921. Jonas D. Mullet married Fanny Stutzman. They have three sons and one daugh
2 CONC ter.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Yoder was married to Elizabeth Helmuth of Holmes County, Ohio, December 25, 1881. To this union eight children were born, five sons and three daughters - as follows.
2 CONT
2 CONT John W. Yoder was married to Sarah Miller, of Holmes County, Ohio, and to this union were born eight children, five sons and three daughters, of whom seven children are living - five sons and two daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT Amanda Yoder was married to Tobias J. Schlabach, and to this union was born twelve children, eight sons and four daughters, of whom nine children are living, seven sons and two daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara Yoder was married to Peter Wagler. To this union were born five children, two sons and three daughters, of whom three are living, two sons and one daughter - twin daughters died.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonas W. Yoder, was married to Amanda Hershberger. No children were born to this union.
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew W. Yoder, was married to Barbara Troyer. To this union were born two children, one son and one daughter, viz. twins. His wife, Barbara, died February 6, 1920.
2 CONT
2 CONT Martin W. Yoder was married to Lovina Yoder. To this union are born three children, one son and two daughters. One daughter died.
2 CONT
2 CONT Menno W. Yoder married Malinda Miller. To this union is born one son.
2 CONT
2 CONT Susanna Yoder married John C. Chupp. To this union are born two children, one son and one daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth, wife of William Yoder, died January 19, 1896 at the age of thirty-five years, ten months and sixteen days.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Yoder was married second time to Barbara Borkholder, of Marshall County - Indiana. To this union were born eight children, two sons and six daughters. One son, William W. Yoder, died October 3, 1910 at the age of four year
2 CONC s, ten months and two days.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel W. Yoder married Elizabeth Burkholder. No children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Yoder married Daniel A. Beachy. To this union is born one daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Yoder married Abraham J. Weaver. No children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine Yoder, single.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Yoder, single.
2 CONT
2 CONT Emma Yoder, single.
2 CONT
2 CONT Magdalena Yoder, single.
2 CONT
2 CONT The descendants of Jonas Yoder, Sr. are - eight children, fifty grandchildren, and sixty-three great grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Given to the best of my ability this fifteenth day of January, 1921, it being my ninetieth birthday.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonas Yoder, Sr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Died May 25, 1924. 93 yrs - 4 mos. - 10 days
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT [ https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/143554606/jonas-yoder ]
