1 NOTE {geni:about_me} MILLERSBURG -- Mary E. (Miller) Hershberger, 92, formerly of Millersburg, and a resident of Walnut Hills Nursing Home, passed away on Monday, Aug. 24, 2015.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born May 5, 1923, in Mount Eaton, to the late Benedict Emmanuel and Katie (Hershberger) Miller. She was a homemaker and later was a clerk in the meat department of Kandels IGA and Plain and Fancy Fabrics in Berlin. In late
2 CONC  summer of 1982, she moved to Sarasota, Fla., where she resided for 24 years before returning to Holmes County.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a member of Bethel Fellowship Church near Berlin and was very compassionate and lived her life with a servant's heart helping family and friends many times during times of illness or by being a great support to them during
2 CONC  difficult times.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are her husband, Sylvanus E. Hershberger, whom she married Dec. 5, 1946; children, Ann (Mel) Mast of Sugarcreek, Paul (Martha) Hershberger of Berlin, Freeman (Verba) Hershberger of Sugarcreek, Katie (Paul) Miller of Balt
2 CONC ic and Regina Moore of New Philadelphia; 13 grandchildren and 23 great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to her parents, she was preceded in death by nine sisters, six brothers, an infant grandchild and an infant great-grandchild.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be Thursday, Aug. 27 at 10 a.m. at Bethel Fellowship Church, 4183 State Route 39, Millersburg, (near Berlin) with Pastor Mark Yoder officiating. Burial will be in the church cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Friends may call today (Tuesday) from 6-8 p.m. or Wednesday from 2-4 and 6-8 p.m. at Bethel Fellowship Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arrangements are being handled by Smith-Varns Funeral Home, Sugarcreek.
