1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John A. N. "Hogback John" Miller, 79, of 12333 Berg Road, Apple Creek, died unexpectedly on Friday, Sept. 27, 2013 in Columbia, Ky. while staying with his daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Maysville on Jan. 16, 1934 to the late Andy and Lizzie Ann (Hershberger) Miller and married Lizzie E. Gingerich on Nov. 26, 1953. She died Dec.19, 1981.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a member of the Old Order Amish Church. He enjoyed working with goats and horses and worked as a laborer most of his life.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by his children, Fannie (Sam) Hershberger of Apple Creek, Barbara (Andy) Yoder of Columbia, Ky., Lydia (Joe) Swartzentruber of Warsaw, Andy (Katie) Miller of Navarre, Eli (Rebecca) Miller of Navarre, Dan (Anna) Mill
2 CONC er of Orrville, Levi (Lizzie) Miller of Orwell, John (Ella) Miller of Navarre, Edward (Mary) Miller of Navarre, Elmer J. Miller of Navarre and Katie (Wayne) Hershberger of Navarre; 68 grandchildren; 62 great-grandchildren and a br
2 CONC other, Dan Miller of Ashland.
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to his parents and wife, he was preceded in death by a daughter, Ada; a grandson; five sisters and two brothers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held on Tuesday at 9:30 a.m. at the Sam Hershberger residence, 7960 Maurer Road, Apple Creek, with Bishop Eli Miller officiating. Burial will be in the Yoder Cemetery near Apple Creek. Friends may call any
2 CONC  time after 2 p.m. on Sunday at the Sam Hershberger residence. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Spidell Funeral Home in Mount Eaton is handling the arrangements.
