1 NOTE {geni:about_me} WOOSTER — Levi Hershberger Jr., 83, of Wooster passed away on Saturday, Feb. 3, 2018, at his home surrounded by his family. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Clarence, N.Y., on April 12, 1934, to the late Levi and Malinda (Miller) Hershberger and married Anna Miller on Oct. 8, 1953. She died June 20, 1994. He then married Esther Hochstetler on Dec. 26, 1997, and she surv
2 CONC ives. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Levi served in alternative services in Columbus from 1953-1956 and was ordained a minister in 1956. He had served as pastor for Pleasant View Mennonite Church near Berlin, Calvary Chapel Mennonite Church near Mount Eaton and Fairl
2 CONC awn Mennonite Church in Apple Creek, retiring in 1995. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He also retired in 2015 from Southeast Local Schools as a bus driver. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Levi was an avid golfer. He studied, taught, played and loved the game. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to his wife, Esther, he is survived by children, Rebecca Gray of Mount Vernon, Priscilla Hershberger of Lakeville, Naomi (Jonas) Troyer of Orrville, Steve (Tammy) Hershberger of Apple Creek, Grace (Bruce) Gerber of Wor
2 CONC thington and Phil (Naz) Hershberger of Wooster; 11 grandchildren; 7 great-grandchildren; and a sister, Mary Miller of Millersburg. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to his first wife, Anna, he was preceded in death by sisters, Edna Burkholder, Ada Hershberger and Katie Miller; and brothers, Noah, Dan and Roman Hershberger. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorial services will be held on Wednesday, Feb. 7, at 11 a.m. at Fairlawn Mennonite Church, 8520 Emerson Road, Apple Creek, with Pastors Duane Detweiler and Steve Bixler officiating. Burial will be held prior in the church cemet
2 CONC ery. Friends may call on Tuesday, Feb. 6, from 2-4 and 6-8 p.m. at the church. Spidell Funeral Home in Mount Eaton is handling the arrangements. 
2 CONT
2 CONT A memorial website has been created by the funeral home and may be accessed at www.spidellfuneralhome.com where you may share a memory or sign the guestbook. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The family would like to thank everyone for their thoughts and prayers and send a special thank you to LifeCare Hospice. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorial contributions may be made to LifeCare Hospice, 1900 Akron Road, Wooster, OH 44691
