1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mary Miller, 85 years old, went home to be with her Savior on Thursday, August 18, 2022, at Majora Lane following a brief illness.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary was born in Clarence, New York on April 5, 1937 to the late Levi and Malinda (Miller) Hershberger. She married Edward Miller on December 30, 1965. They celebrated 27 years of marriage before Edward passed on October 8, 1993.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary was determined and hard working in all she did. She received her GED in her late 30’s and soon after took classes to obtain her Certified Dietary Manager license. She worked in food service most of her working career, and had
2 CONC  role of manager over a variety of kitchens. Mary worked at Bob’s Drive Thru, Bird’s Nest, Castle Nursing Homes, Altercare, and retired from Southeast local school as dietary manager at Holmesville Elementary. She also cooked at t
2 CONC he Holmes County Senior Center after her retirement from the school.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary had the gift of hospitality. She loved having friends and family in for meals and took pride in what she made. She especially loved making her family’s favorite foods at the holiday’s and any other get togethers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary was a member of New Pointe church, Millersburg, where she had been in a small group of ladies who were all so special to her. She loved all kinds of music; mostly praise & worship. She enjoyed going with her friend, Ruth, to 
2 CONC listen to Music on the Square in Berlin during the summers. Mary also loved having lunch dates with her special friends: Sandra, Marilyn and Nancy. She loved to travel ; loved making the best cinnamon rolls for family and friends;
2 CONC  and she loved to laugh. Many times in her last years of life she would say “what would we do if we couldn’t laugh”. Most importantly, Mary loved her family and time spent with them; and she loved the Lord.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are children, Robin (Ken) Allison of Houston, Texas, Wendell (Julie) Miller of Montgomery, Texas, Sheila (Bob) Turner of Glenmont, and Tammy (Mike) Judson of Killbuck; 7 grandchildren; 16 great grandchildren, which inclu
2 CONC des a great granddaughter due to arrive February 2023.
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to her husband, Edward, Mary was preceded in death by her daughter, Ann Keesler; sisters, Edna Burkholder, Ada Hershberger, Katie Miller, and brothers Noah, Dan, Roman and Levi Hershberger.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be held Monday, August 22 at 2 pm at Alexander Funeral Home, Millersburg. Burial will be held immediately following the service at Sherwood Memorial Gardens, Wooster. Friends may call on the same day, prior to the se
2 CONC rvice, from 12- 2 pm.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family would like to thank everyone for their thoughts and prayers these last few weeks of Mary’s illness. Special thank you’s to the staff at Majora Lane and LifeCare Hospice , who all took such great care of Mary. And thank 
2 CONC you to Millersburg Davita for treating Mary like family during the last 4 years of receiving dialysis treatments there.
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorial contributions may be made to LifeCare Hospice, 1900 Akron Rd, Wooster, OH 44691.
2 CONT
2 CONT Posted online on August 19, 2022
2 CONT
2 CONT Published in The Daily Record
