2 CONT <p><span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'Source Sans Pro', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;">Vernon G. Zurcher, 68, Berne, former varsity boys basketball coach at Adams Central High Sc
2 CONC hool, died Wednesday in Fajardo, Puerto Rico, of an apparent heart attack.</span><br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'Source Sans Pro', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #
2 CONC fafafa;" /><br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'Source Sans Pro', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px;background-color: #fafafa;" /><span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'Source Sans Pro',
2 CONC  Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;">Mr. Zurcher was attending an insurance seminar in Puerto Rico at the time of his death. An agent for the Columbus Life Insurance Company, he was a motivat
2 CONC ional speaker, a group coordinator for Zurcher's Tire, Inc., Monroe, and had previously coached and taught at Larwill and Wawasee High School in addition to Adams Central.</span><br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; f
2 CONC ont-family: 'Source Sans Pro', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;" /><br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'Source Sans Pro', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size
2 CONC : 15px; background-color: #fafafa;" /><span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'Source Sans Pro', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;">A member of First Missionary Church, Berne, he was a Sun
2 CONC day School teacher at the church and was a former president of the Swiss Heritage Society.</span><br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'Source Sans Pro', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; bac
2 CONC kground-color: #fafafa;" /><br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'Source Sans Pro', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;" /><span style="color: #36322d; font-family: '
2 CONC Source Sans Pro', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;">Born in Adams County on January 2, 1929, Mr. Zurcher was the son of William and Eva Stauffer-Zurcher. He married Vera Inniger on January 
2 CONC 2, 1950; she survives. Also surviving are four sons: Steven, Berne; Michael, Fort Wayne; Robin, Leesburg; and Kim, Plano, Texas; a daughter, Mrs. Brian (Melanie) Williams of Nappanee; two brothers, Paul and Joshua, both of Monroe;
2 CONC  two sisters, Gladys Nussbaum and Naomi Macy, both of Berne, and ninegrandchildren.</span><br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'Source Sans Pro', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background
2 CONC -color: #fafafa;" /><br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'Source Sans Pro', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;" /><span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'Source 
2 CONC Sans Pro', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;">Two brothers, Dale and Arthur, preceded him in death.</span><br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'Source Sans Pro', H
2 CONC elvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;" /><br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'Source Sans Pro', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafaf
2 CONC a;" /><span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'Source Sans Pro', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;">Funeral services will be held at 2 p.m. Sunday at First Missionary Church , Berne, and a
2 CONC  private family burial service will be held at Evangelical Mennonite Church Cemetery, Berne. Calling will be from noonto 9 pm. at Yager-Kirchhofer Funeral Home, Berne. Preferred memorials are to the First Missionary Church Buildin
2 CONC g Fund or to the Children's Orphanage in Haiti.</span><br style="box-sizing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'Source Sans Pro', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;" /><br style="box-s
2 CONC izing: border-box; color: #36322d; font-family: 'Source Sans Pro', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;" /><span style="color: #36322d; font-family: 'Source Sans Pro', Helvetica, Arial, sans-se
2 CONC rif; font-size: 15px; background-color: #fafafa;">(Editor's note: This obituary notice is being reprinted to provide additional information and corrections in information given to the Democrat for Thursday's obituary notice)</span
2 CONC ></p>
