1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Obituary delivered at Ellen's funeral:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Ellen Egly, daughter of Jacob and Lydia Egly, was born near Berne, Ind., November 7, 1873 and departed this life at the home of her daughter near Chenoa, Ill., Saturday afternoon September 27, 1941, aged 67 years 10 months 20 day
2 CONC s.  She had been in ill health for the last year and a half, but seriously ill the past month.
2 CONT
2 CONT At the age of 14, she accepted the Lord as her personal Saviour under the preaching of her grandfather Bishop Henry Egly.  She became a member of the Defenseless Mennonite Church near Leo, Indiana.
2 CONT
2 CONT On December 14, 1893, she was united in marriage to Michael Ulrich, who preceded her in death April 16, 1922.  To this union were born four daughters and three sons, of whom two daughters and one son preceded her in death.
2 CONT
2 CONT On June 7, 1928, she was married to C. K. Ulrich, who's death occured on October 30, 1937.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are two daughters, Mrs. Wilda Zehr near Chenoa, Ill.,  Mrs. Inez Zehr, near Gridley, Ill., Two sons, Villas of Montpelier, Ohio, and Arthur of Pioneer, Ohio; three sisters, Mrs. Emma Oyer of Chenoa, Ill., Mrs. Mary Moser
2 CONC , of Woodburn, Ind., Mrs. Fann Kopp, Peoria, Ill., One brother, Sam, near Berne, Ind., and seventeen grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her life was an exempliary Christian one.  It was not without trials and sorrow, but it seemed they never discouraged her.  She met them bravely for she knew the God she served would take care of her.  She was a good mother and we
2 CONC  believe loved by everyone that knew her.
2 CONT
2 CONT We never knew her to be selfish.  She always sought the welfare of others and would deny herself of necessities if need be."
2 CONT
2 CONT [After Michael's death, Ellen married his first cousin, Chris K. Ulrich, a widower with 10 children.  Ellen helped raise Chris' 4 youngest children.  Thus, Ellen's natural children were related to Ellen's stepchildren (second cous
2 CONC ins) and according to Inez Ulrich, the family frequently was very confusing to non-family members].
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/32259698/ellen-ulrich Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 16 2023, 18:17:16 UTC''
