1 NOTE {geni:about_me} (Obit from Adams County, Indiana Historical Society Scrapbook)
2 CONT
2 CONT (Handwritten date:  Monday, June 19, 1939)
2 CONT
2 CONT MRS. KATE RICH DIES FRIDAY
2 CONT Sister of Samuel Egly Dies at Home in Allen County
2 CONT
2 CONT    Mrs. Kate Rich, 61, of Milan twp., Allen county, died at 4:45 p.m. Friday at the home of her daughter, Mrs. Garnet Gerig, also of Milan twp.  She had suffered a paralytic stroke Sunday, June 11.  Surviving are two other daughte
2 CONC rs, Mrs. Hazel Poe of Indianapolis and Miss Ruby Rich;  four sisters, Mrs. Ellen Ulrich of Flanagan, Ill., Mrs. Emma Oyer of Chenoa, Ill., Mrs. Mary Moser of Woodburn and Mrs. Fannie Kopp of Peoria, Ill.;  two brothers, Samuel Egl
2 CONC y of Berne, and Milo Egly of Pittsburgh, Pa., and three grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT    Funeral services were held at 1:30 p.m. Sunday (CST) at the Rich home and at 2 p.m. (CST) at the Defenseless Mennonite church, the Rev. J. H. Sauder officiating.  Burial was in the Leo cemetery.* Reference: [https://www.findagr
2 CONC ave.com/memorial/143617634/kate-rich Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 16 2023, 18:17:16 UTC''
