1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Decatur Daily Democrat, Adams County, IN  Monday, Jan. 6, 1975
2 CONT                                               Albert Egly
2 CONT
2 CONT             Funeral services were held at 1 p.m. today for a former Berne banker, Albert Egly, 95, of Terre Haute, who died at 5:30 p.m. Thursday in Union hospital, Terre Haute.  Burial was in the Leo cemetery.  The C.M. Sloan & S
2 CONC ons funeral home was in charge of arrangements and the funeral was held there.
2 CONT
2 CONT             A former resident of Berne and then of Fort Wayne, Egly was a retired banker, attorney and accountant who organized Grabill State Bank in 1906 and the New home Telephone Company.
2 CONT
2 CONT             He was also an organizer of Allen County Electric Light and Power Co. which served northeast Allen County, and had an accounting service in Fort Wayne before suffering a stroke in 1969.  He moved at that time to the ho
2 CONC me of his son, Dr. Richard Egly, in Terre Haute.
2 CONT
2 CONT             A native of Geneva, he attended school at Valparaiso University and at the age of 19 taught at the Summer session there.  He later graduated from Ormsby-Rinehart Business College, Bluffton.
2 CONT
2 CONT             Mr. Egly was assistant cashier of the Peoples State Bank, Berne, before organizing State Bank of Grabill in 1906, as its cashier and president for 20 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT             He was elder emeritus of the First Christian church (Disciples of Christ), Fort Wayne, and had been a former active member of Central Lions Club, and was quite active in Izaak Walton League, Acres, Inc., and the Anthon
2 CONC y Wayne Stamp Club.
2 CONT
2 CONT             Surviving in addition to the son is one sister, Mrs. Raymond Filer of Geneva.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/86452994/albert-egly Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 16 2023, 7:07:59 UTC''
