1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Age 84
2 CONT
2 CONT William Henry Egly, Associate Professor of English in the College of Engineering, is relinquishing his active duties after forty years of teaching at The University of Michigan. 
2 CONT
2 CONT A graduate of the College of Literature, Science, and the Arts in the Class of 1913, he returned to University summer sessions while serving as a high school principal and as a teacher at Bluffton College, and joined the staff of 
2 CONC the College of Engineering upon earning his master's degree. His interests being various, he continued his graduate study in both English and sociology; he was concerned with literature both as art and as social commentary. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Through informal reading, he acquired also a wide knowledge of science generally. His example, which was recommended by his personal generosity and warmth, proved infectious; he engendered in his students the desire to broaden the
2 CONC ir own cultural and intellectual backgrounds. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Professor Egly's fellows in the College of Engineering are sensitive to the loss of a stimulating teacher and a friendly and co-operative colleague.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Regents of the University, now conferring on him the title Associate Professor Emeritus of English, profoundly thank him for his many years of able service and cordially extend to him the privileges which are his due.
2 CONT
2 CONT Regents' Proceedings, June 1960, Page 1273* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/110320508/william-henry-egly Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 16 2023, 7:07:59 UT
2 CONC C''
