1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Illness Fatal to Mrs. Egly, 76
2 CONT  Mrs. Anna Egly, 76, died at 8:25 o'clock Monday night at 
2 CONT her home, 1118 West Jefferson Street, after an extended 
2 CONT illness. She was a member of the First Presbyterian Church 
2 CONT and a lifelong resident of Allen County. She had lived in Fort 
2 CONT Wayne for the last 24 years.
2 CONT  Surviving are her husband, Christian G. Egly; two 
2 CONT daughters, Mrs. Guy C. Latchew of Chicago and Mrs. Dan H. 
2 CONT Tyndall of Decatur; one son, Henry D. Egly of Willoughby, O.; 
2 CONT two sisters, Mrs. Catherine Garig and Mrs. Lydia Souder of 
2 CONT Allen County, and six granddaughters.
2 CONT  The body was removed to the Chalfant, Perry& Pook Funeral
2 CONT Home, where the body may be viewed after 4 o'clock this 
2 CONT afternoon. Funeral services will be held at 1 o'clock 
2 CONT Wednesday afternoon at the funeral home and at 2:30 o'clock
2 CONT at the Mennonite Church, Berne. Rev. George William Allison 
2 CONT of the First Presbyterian Church, Fort Wayne and Rev. Suckau,
2 CONT Berne officiating. Burial will be in the Berne Cemetery.
2 CONT Journal-Gazette, Allen County, Indiana
2 CONT Tuesday, September 3, 1940
2 CONT **
