1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Decatur Daily Democrat, Adams County, IN
2 CONT Thursday, January 24, 1974
2 CONT
2 CONT Kathryn Tyndall, 81, dies today at Kokomo; services are Saturday
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Kathryn E. Tyndall, 81, formerly of 404 Stratton Way and widow of Daniel H. Tyndall, died at 5:40 a.m. this morning in Turtle Creek Convalescent Home, Kokomo, following an extended illness.
2 CONT
2 CONT The well-known lady, a prominent vocalist in this area for half a century, was a member of the first United Methodist Church, the music department of the Woman’s Club, Research Club, Tri Kappa, and was a 50-year member of the Orde
2 CONC r of Eastern Star. She was a past matron of the Eastern Star, past grand Esther, and past district deputy of district 14 in that organization.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Berne on September 25, 1892, she was the daughter of Christian G. and Anna Shanebeck-Egly, and was married on August 16, 1916, to Daniel H. Tyndall, a Decatur businessman, who died Feb. 21, 1973. My Tyndall was associated 
2 CONC with the Krick-Tyndall Tile Company.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are two daughters, Mrs. Chalmer (Mary Kathryn) Denny of Kokomo, and Mrs. Cloyd W. (Anna Jane) Rucker of Arlington, Rex.; one sister, Mrs. Lillian Latchaw of Findlay, O.; four grandchildren, Judith D. Firme, Nancy Rucker,
2 CONC  Anna Kathryn Herndon and Robert B. Rucker, and two great-grandchildren. One brother preceded her in death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held at 2 p.m. Saturday at the Winteregg-Linn and Haggard funeral home, with Rev. Harold Leininger officiating. Burial will be in the Decatur cemetery. Friends may call at the funeral home after 4 p.m. Fri
2 CONC day. The Order of Eastern Star will hold services at 7:30 p.m. Friday.
2 CONT Contributor: Karin King (47469179) •
2 CONT **
2 CONT
2 CONT Kokomo Tribune, Kokomo, Indiana; Thursday, January 24, 1974
2 CONT MRS. KATHRYN TYNDALL
2 CONT Mrs. Kathryn Tyndall, 81, formerly of Decatur, died at 5:40 a.m. Thursday in Turtle Creek Convalescent Centre.
2 CONT Born September 26, 1892, she was the daughter of Christian and Anna Egly.  She was married in 1915 to Daniel Tyndall who preceded her in death in 1973.
2 CONT She was a member of the First United Methodist Church, the Women's Music Club, Research Club, Tri Kappa Sorority, all in Decatur.  She was a 50-year member of the Eastern Star and past grand Esther of Indiana.
2 CONT Surviving are a daughter, Mrs. Chalmer (Mary Kay) Denny of Kokomo and Mrs. Cloyd W. (Anna June) Rucker, of Arlington, Tex.; a sister, Mrs. Lillian Latchaw of Findley, Ohio; four grandchildren and two great-grandchildren.
2 CONT Funeral services will be at 2 p.m. Saturday in Winter, Egg and Linn  [sic] Funeral Home of Decatur, with the Rev. Harold Leininger officiating.  Burial will be in Decatur Cemetery.  Friends may call after 4 p.m. Friday.* Reference
