1 NOTE {geni:about_me} s/o William Bounds Sr. & Beulah (Irwin)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st.....Spouse Stella Harriett (Egly)
2 CONT
2 CONT Known Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mark, Steve, & Angela Bounds
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd Spouse....Julia E. (Carr)...married June 20, 1958 St. Paul, Minnesota
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT Personal info from family member
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary
2 CONT 13 Nov 2014
2 CONT DANVILLE – William "Bill" Best Bounds Jr., 90, of Danville passed away on Tuesday (Nov. 11, 2014) at Presence United Samaritans Medical Center in Danville.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bill was born on Aug. 3, 1924, in Blanchard, Okla., the son of William and Beulah (Irwin) Bounds Sr. He married Julia E. Carr on June 20, 1958, in St. Paul, Minn. She preceded him in death on June 26, 2008.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bill will be deeply missed by his two sons, Stephen Bounds of Danville and Mark (Susan) Bounds of Danville; one daughter, Angela (Mark) Hodgson of Oakwood; several grandchildren, great-grandchildren, nieces and nephews; one brothe
2 CONC r-in-law, Pat (Martha) Carr of Villa Grove; one sister-in-law and best friend, Carmen "Sue" Carr of Danville; and many great friends, too numerous to list.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bill was preceded in death by his parents; wife, Julia; one brother, Stanley Bounds; and two sisters, Shirley Patterson and Jackie York.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bill proudly served in the U.S. Navy. He began his career as a truck driver for Denver Chicago, and the old Halls Freight Lines. Bill later went to work for the late James R. Hoffa, in the 1960s, as a union organizer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bill continued his career with the Teamsters Union Local 26 in Danville as a business agent. He later was elected president of Local 26 and held that position for 30 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bill was also the president of the Teamsters Joint Council 65 located in Springfield for approximately 18 years, overseeing parts of four states and 30,000 members.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bill served on many boards in Vermilion County, including CRIS Senior Services, Vermilion County Airport Authority, Labor Management Council and Vermilion County Animal Shelter. He was a past member of the Knights of Columbus and 
2 CONC Moose Lodge. Bill was a member of St. Paul's Catholic Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bill had a love for all animals, for which he opened his heart and home, especially his dog Missy. He loved sports and country music, especially his idol George Jones. Bill loved singing and enjoyed recording several songs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bill's family wishes to thank Becky Hathaway for years of service helping Bill, Paul Offutt, a special friend who was instrumental in Bill's health care at The Cleveland Clinic, and Dr. Bobat for his care and compassion.
2 CONT
2 CONT A celebration of Bill's life will be held at 10:30 a.m. Saturday, Nov. 15, 2014, at Sunset Funeral Home and Cremation Center in Danville, with the Rev. Greg Nelson officiating. Visitation will be held from 4 to 8 p.m. Friday, Nov.
2 CONC  14, 2014, at the funeral home. Entombment will take place at Sunset Memorial Park.
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorials can be made in Bill's name to C.A.R.A. No Kill Shelter, Danville Humane Society or a veterans' charity of the donor's choice. Please join Bill's family in sharing photos, videos and memories of him through his tribute wa
2 CONC ll at www.sunsetfuneralhome.com.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/138652848/william-best-bounds Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 17 2023, 18:53:30 UTC''
