2 DATE 6 AUG 1951
2 PLAC Danville, Vermilion County, Illinois, USA
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 14 DEC 2020
2 PLAC Danville, Vermilion County, Illinois, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mark W. Bounds, 69, of Danville, Illinois, peacefully passed away at 12:24 A.M.,  December 14, 2020, in the comfort of his home, with his wife Susan by his side.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mark was born on August 6, 1951 in Danville, Illinois to William (Bill) and Harriet (Egly) Bounds. Mark married Susan (Slayton) on May 18, 1996 and they enjoyed a wonderful 24 year marriage and were looking forward to traveling. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mark is survived by his loving and devoted wife Susan; his brother, Steve Bounds of Danville, Illinois; brother-in-law, Mark Hodgson of Oakwood, Illinois; sister-in-law, Kathy (Charlie) Coulter of La Quinta, California; "sister-in
2 CONC -law" Becky Engel of Danville, Illinois and several aunts and uncles, cousins, nieces and nephews.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by his father, William (Bill) Bounds; his mother, Harriet Hewitt; step mother, Julia Bounds; sister, Angela Hodgson; in-laws, Ted Sr. and Betty Slayton and brother-in-law, Ted Slayton, Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mark was a graduate of DHS class of '69.  His senior year he became a proud member of the Country Youngin's band and played many venues throughout the community.  Mark worked for a time with his father, Bill Bounds, at the Teamste
2 CONC rs Local 26 in Danville, and later became a locomotive engineer for CSX Transportation, from which he retired. Mark enjoyed watching sports, grilling and cooking, playing guitar and singing country classics (no doubt a talent he i
2 CONC nherited from his father, Bill), dancing with Susan, taking care of his yard, many good times with family and friends, and loved his cat Charlie. He was spiritual and enjoyed Sunday morning worship within his home. Mark valiantly 
2 CONC fought cancer since March of 2020.  He had so many great friends, neighbors, and family, and their unfailing support through this difficult time as been a steady source of solace and comfort to both Mark and Susan.  
2 CONT
2 CONT From one of Mark's favorite hymns....
2 CONT
2 CONT "And then one day, I'll cross the river and fight life's final war with pain. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  And then as death gives way to victory, I'll see the lights of glory, and I'll know he reigns."
2 CONT
2 CONT Cremation rites have been entrusted to Sunset Funeral Home and Cremation Center in Danville, Illinois, 3940 N Vermilion St. Danville, Illinois 61834.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/219872726/mark-w-bounds Find A 
2 CONC Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 17 2023, 18:53:30 UTC''
