2 CONT Personally knew her & Mark Hodgson
2 CONT Cremated∼Angela S. Hodgson, 62, of Oakwood, died at 6:00 a.m., Tuesday, May 5, 2015, at Carle Foundation Hospital in Urbana from medical complications.
2 CONT Angela was born September 3, 1952, in Danville, IL, and lived in Oakwood, IL for the last 30 years. 
2 CONT She enjoyed boating, camping, barbecuing, and spending time with friends and family. In the last few years she especially enjoyed helping the elderly people that she cleaned houses for. She was a caring person who didn’t know a st
2 CONC ranger.
2 CONT She is survived by her Husband Mark Hodgson, her sons Jason Geiling and Justin Behrens, her step son Brandon Hodgson, her step daughter Andrea Hodgson, her grandson Blake Behrens, and her brothers Mark and Steve Bounds.
2 CONT She was preceded in death by her parents Bill Bounds and Harriet Hewitt (Egly)
2 CONT A celebration of Angela’s life will be held on Saturday, April 9, 2015 at 2:00 PM at Sunset Funeral Home and Cremation Center in Danville with Pastor Jay Johnson officiating. Visitation will be held on Friday, April 8, 2015 from 4
2 CONC :00-8:00 PM at Sunset Funeral Home. Please join Angela’s family in sharing photos, videos and memories on her tribute wall at www.sunsetfuneralhome.com* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/146068462/angela-suzanne-hodg
