1 NOTE {geni:about_me} BEULAH L. EGLY, 95, passed away Thursday, Feb. 5, 2015, at Meadowbrook Manor, Naperville, Ill. Born in Fort Wayne, Beulah was an accounts payable clerk with Essex Interna tional for three years, retiring in 1978. S
2 CONC he was a member of First Missionary Church. Surviving are her daughter, Marjorie Eisenacher of Warrenville, Ill.; four grandchildren; eight great-grandchildren; sister, Erma M. Goyer of Fort Wayne; nephew, John (Bernice) Augsburge
2 CONC r; three great nieces and great nephews; and four great-great-nieces and great-great-nephews. She was preceded in death by husband, Carl Egly; son, Keith Egly; and parents, Harry and Louisa (Drake) Jackson. Service is 11 a.m. Sund
2 CONC ay, Feb. 15, 2015, at D.O. McComb & Sons Covington Knolls Funeral Home, 8325 Covington Road, with calling one hour prior. The Rev. Jim Johnson officiating. Calling also from 3 to 5 and 7 to 9 p.m. Saturday, Feb. 14, 2015, at the f
2 CONC uneral home. Burial in Covington Memorial Gardens. Memorials may be made to First Missionary Church.
