1 NOTE {geni:about_me} MAYSVILLE -- Katie Ann (ne Wengerd) Hilty, 94, of Maysville, passed away peacefully with her family at her side on Saturday, Feb. 18, 2017, following a brief illness. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born in Wayne County on Oct. 20, 1922, to Noah and Katie Ann (ne Miller) Wengerd. Katie married Menno E. Hilty on Dec. 11, 1947. He died Feb. 12, 1977. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She had made her home in Maysville for 49 years and was a member of the Old Order Amish Church. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by two sons and five daughters, Anna (John Byler) of Holmesville, Clara (Levi Shetler) of Fredericksburg, Emma (Dan Hershberger) of Apple Creek, Irvin (Nancy) Hilty of Apple Creek, Edna (Eli Yoder) of Adamsville, L
2 CONC aura (Levi Hostetler) of Wooster and Marvin (Emma) Hilty of the home; 56 grandchildren; 110 great-grandchildren; 1 great-great-grandchild; and a brother-in-law, Enos Byler. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to her husband and parents, she was preceded in death by her stepmother; two sons; two brothers; six sisters; two grandchildren; and a great-grandchild. 
2 CONT
2 CONT A funeral service will be 9 a.m. Tuesday, Feb. 21, 2017, at the family residence, with Bishop Roman Eicher officiating. Burial will follow in the Hershberger Cemetery, Paint Township, Wayne County. Friends may call anytime at the 
2 CONC family residence. Spidell Funeral Home in Mount Eaton is handling the arrangements. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The family extends their sincere thanks to the staff of LifeCare Hospice for the wonderful care given to their mother and grandmother.
