1 NOTE {geni:about_me} APPLE CREEK -- Atlee A. Hershberger, 69, of 10380 Harrison Road, Apple Creek (Maysville), died Wednesday, Dec. 30, 2015 at Akron General Medical Center following a period of declining health.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born near Fredericksburg on Dec. 23, 1946 to the late Andy E. and Elizabeth D. (Hostetler) Hershberger and married Mandy M. Hilty on Nov. 25, 1971. She survives.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a member of the Old Order Amish Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to his wife, he is survived by children, Robert (Linda) Hershberger of Fredericksburg, Roy (Anna Marie) Hershberger of Dundee, Mervin (Miriam) Hershberger and Michael (Ada) Hershberger, both of Apple Creek; 18 grandchi
2 CONC ldren; brothers, Ray and Nevin (Rosie) of Fredericksburg, Andy Jr. (Betty) and Vernon (Barbara) of Apple Creek and Owen (Amanda) of Millersburg; sisters, Mary (Jim) Miller of Wooster, Mabel (Simon) Yoder of Apple Creek and Irene (
2 CONC Pete) Weaver of Fredericksburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to his parents, he was preceded in death by brothers, Paul and Ervin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held today (Saturday) at 9 a.m. at the family residence with Bishop Martin J. Yoder officiating. Burial will follow in the Hershberger Family Cemetery in Paint Township, Wayne County. Friends may call anyt
2 CONC ime at the family residence. Spidell Funeral Home in Mount Eaton is handling the arrangements.
