1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ELIZABETH ZEHR, 96, died Sunday, Sept. 5, 2010, at The Cedars, Leo. Born in Daviess County. She spent much of her life sharing with and caring for others. She spent over 55 years at the Fort Wayne Rescue Mission, w
2 CONC orking in the clothing store and teaching a childrens Sunday school class. She also shared her late husband, Amos' vision working with International Child Care and the Grace Childrens Hospital, Port Au Prince, Haiti. Survivors inc
2 CONC lude sons, Joseph (Tammera) Zehr of Fort Wayne and David (Debra) Zehr of Leo; grandchildren, Eric (Debroah) Zehr, Lisa (James) Morlan, Amy (Paul) McIntosh, Michelle (Chance) Baldwin, Joshua Zehr, and Caleb Zehr; and 10 great-grand
2 CONC children. Funeral service is 3 p.m. Wednesday at Central Church, 5801 Schwartz Road, with calling from 1 to 3 p.m. The Rev. Don Delagrange officiating. Burial in Yaggy Cementery, Grabill. Arrangements by D.O. McComb & Sons Pine Va
2 CONC lley Park Funeral Home, 1320 Dupont Road. Memorials to the Fort Wayne Rescue Mission. 
