1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Cornelius "Neal" J. Eash Cornelius "Neal" J. Eash, 87, of Shipshewana, died at 8:06 PM on Tuesday, January 11, 2011 at Parkview LaGrange  Hospital, Lagrange. He was born on September 7, 1923 in LaGrange County, to 
2 CONC John H. and Ida (Beachy) Eash. On  December 30, 1954 he married Ruth Graber, she died September 30, 1969. On November 25, 1970 he married Wilma  Slabaugh, she survives. Survivors in addition to his wife are four daughters, Rosanna
2 CONC  (Andrew, Jr.) Yoder of  Shipshewana, Wilma (Dave) Anderson of Nappanee, Naomi (Ervin) Raber and Christina (Lonnie) Miller both of  Shipshewana; four sons, Melvin (Laura) Eash of Lagrange, Marion (Susan) Eash of Nappanee, Sylvan (
2 CONC Connie) Eash of  Goshen, Allen (Cindy) Eash of Middlebury; 37 grandchildren, 33 great grandchildren; sister, Katie (Dan) Hochstetler of  Topeka; sister-in-law Polly Eash of Shipshewana; He was preceded in death by his first wife, 
2 CONC both parents, daughter,  Pauline Eash, two grandsons, Andrew and Austin Graber, four brothers, Levi, Tobe, Lewis, and Eli Eash, four sisters,  Lena Bontrager, Fannie Frey, Esther Bontrager, Lucy Eash. He was a member of the Old Or
2 CONC der Amish Church, had worked  maintenance at the Davis Mercantile and area factories and did shoe repair. Visitation will be after 3:00 PM on Wednesday  January 12, and all day Thursday, January 13, at the Lonnie Miller residence,
2 CONC  2030 N. 500 W. Shipshewana. Funeral  services will be at 9:30 AM on Friday January 14, at the LaVern Beechy residence, 5580 W. 200, Shipshewana. Services will  be conducted by Bishop Menno Petersheim and home ministers. Burial wi
2 CONC ll be in East Barren Cemetery, Shipshewana.  Online condolences may be sent at millerstewartfuneralhome.com.
