1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Victor Eicher Sr., 80, of Athens Township, passed away on November 9, 2020 at Bronson Battle Creek Hospital. Funeral services will take place at 9:00 AM on Thursday, November 12, 2020 at the Levi Delagrange residen
2 CONC ce, 3837 S Drive South, Athens, MI 49011. Visitation will take place Tuesday, November 10, 2020 afternoon and all day on Wednesday, November 11, 2020 at the Levi Delagrange residence. Interment will take place at Burlington Old Or
2 CONC der Amish Cemetery in Burlington Township. The family is being served by Lighthouse Funeral & Cremation in Union City. Victor was born on October 25, 1940 to Henry and Maggie (Graber) Eicher in Grabil, IN. On October 25, 1962 he m
2 CONC arried Catherine Graber in Camden, MI. She preceded him in death in 2010. He was a member of the Old Order Amish Church. Surviving Victor are his children, Esther (Jonas) Brenneman, Silas Eicher, Naomi (Sam) Steury, Rosa (Nicholas
2 CONC ) Graber, Barbara (Levi) Delagrange, Victor (Eileen) Eicher Jr. Lavina (Ben) Delagrange, Keturah (Sam) Delagrange, Priscilla (David) Schwartz, 73 grandchildren, 49, great-grandchildren, 9 siblings, many nieces, nephews and other f
2 CONC amily. He was preceded in death by his parents, wife, daughter Maggie, daughter-in-law, Naomi, one sister, one grandchild and one great-grandchild.
