2 CONC y, blessed be God, do this eighteenth day of November, in the year of our Lord 1760, make and order this my last Will and Testament, in manner following, that is to say: First, I give and bequeath to Augnis, my wife, the stone end
2 CONC  of my dwelling house for her to live in, as also 2 cows and a young horse , with a sufficiency of hay yearly to fodder said creatures, with four sheep and sufficiency of hay yearly to fodder said sheep, as also my Sd wife's saddl
2 CONC e she is to possess and enjoy. And next, I give and bequeath to this my Sd wife's daughter, Barbara Frets, seven pounds, the remainder of ten pounds, which I have engaged to pay her. I also allow and bequeath to my son, Martin Ove
2 CONC rhold, the sum of ten pounds to be levied of my estate. I give and be bequeath to my daughter, Mary a new suit of in full, a bed and bedding of cloaths with a bedstead, a cow, a tub, a pail, a churn, pewter, an iron pot and frying
2 CONC  pan. I also give and bequeath to my first wife's three daughters, Elise, wife of Wm. Tyson, Ann, wife of Joseph Tyson, Katherine, wife of Benjamin Hendricks, and William, son of my second wife, and my daughter Madaline, wife of J
2 CONC acob Frets, and daughter of my second wife: as also I bequeah to Elizabeth, Joseph and Abraham, children of my now present wife, with my first wife's children, an equal part of the remainder of my estate, after the first above men
