1 OCCU Farmer
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/30511035/jacob-kratz
2 CONT
2 CONT KRATZ.-On the 23rd of Feb. 1903, in Bucks Co., Pa., of the infirmities of old age, Bro. Jacob Kratz, aged 88 Y., 8 M., 20 D. He was born on the 3rd of June 1814, in the same neighborhood where he lived all his life and where he di
2 CONC ed. During his earlier years he taught school during the winter, while his summers were spent on the farm. He was a model Christian and a faithful exponent and defender of the principles of our Mennonite common faith and doctrine.
2 CONC  He was a devoted Christian, kind, charitable and honest in all his dealings, and was always ready to give full value for everything he bought. During his last years his conversation was about spiritual things. In the blessed hope
2 CONC  of the life to come his lamp of life went out on earth to shine anew in the realms of glory. Three children - Salome, wife of John F. Funk of Elkhart, Ind., H.M., residing on the old homestead, and Annie, wife of Joseph D. Bishop
2 CONC  - three grandchildren and four great-grandchildren survive him. he was buried on the 27th at Blooming Glen, the place where during the whole period of his life he attended the services of God's house. Services were conducted by B
2 CONC ishop. H.D. Rosen
2 CONT
2 CONT A Brief History of Jacob Wismer and a Complete Genealogical Family Register With Biographies of His Descendants from the Earliest Available Records to the Present Time By A J Fretz, Eli Wismer 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://books.google.com/books?id=nwBgAAAAMAAJ 
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 30
2 CONT
2 CONT VI. Mary Meyers, bn. Mar. 7, 1818. Mrd. Jacob Kratz, Nov. 28, 1838. He was bn. June 3, 1814. P. O., Dublin, Pa. Farmer. Menn. Children: Salome, Henry, Anna, Isaiah.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Title: Bookplate (Bücherzeichen) for Jacob Kratz
2 CONT
2 CONT Category: Bookplate (Bücherzeichen)
2 CONT
2 CONT Creators:  Decorator: [Jacob Oberholtzer (1794-1880)]  Scrivener: [Jacob Oberholtzer (1794-1880)]
2 CONT
2 CONT Creation Place:  Town/Township: Hilltown School, Hilltown Township  County: Bucks  State/Province: Pennsylvania  Note: Based on inscription on document
2 CONT
2 CONT Creation Date: 2/27/1823
2 CONT
2 CONT Physical Description: Leaf
2 CONT
2 CONT Dimensions: 9.6 cm x 16 cm
2 CONT
2 CONT Material: Laid paper; watercolor; ink
2 CONT
2 CONT Media Type: Manuscripts
2 CONT
2 CONT Language: German
2 CONT
2 CONT Scripts/Text: Fraktur; German script
2 CONT
2 CONT Associated Names: Kratz, Jacob; Oberholtzer, Jacob
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hand-drawn; hand-colored; hand-lettered. The text in Fraktur and German script is in the center of the document. It is flanked on each side by a leafy, tree-like plant with various flowers. The entire document is framed by a decor
2 CONC ative border. This bookplate is in the tune book for which it was made.  (PA GER Borneman 48)
2 CONT
2 CONT Two schoolmasters entered tunes in the booklet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Transcription:
2 CONT
2 CONT Dieses \ Harmonische Melodeyen \ Büchlein Gehöret \ Jacob Kratz  Sing Schüler in der \ Hilltauner Schule Geschrieb= \ ben d. 27 ten Hornung \ Im Jahr 1823.
2 CONT
2 CONT Translation:
2 CONT
2 CONT This little harmonious melody book belongs to Jacob Kratz, singing student in the Hilltown School. Written the 27th of February in the year 1823.
2 CONT
2 CONT Provenance:  Henry S. Borneman
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliography:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Jacob Oberholtzer" in  Cory M. Amsler, ed., Bucks County Fraktur (Kutztown, Pa.: Pennsylvania German Society, 1999), pp. 280-283; published as fig. 249 on p. 281.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Jane Lederach Hershey, "The Notenbüchlein Tradition in Eastern Pennsylvania Mennonite Community Schools," in  Cory M. Amsler, ed., Bucks County Fraktur (Kutztown, Pa.: Pennsylvania German Society, 1999), p. 143.
2 CONT
2 CONT Weiser Number: 200
2 CONT
2 CONT http://libwww.freelibrary.org/fraktur/tour.cfm
