1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT 1820-010011/00101
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Jacob Shut 1817, probated 1825 :Muhlenberg County, Kentucky
2 CONT
2 CONT ****************************************************************************
2 CONT USGENWEB NOTICE: In keeping with our policy of providing free genealogical
2 CONT information on the Internet, data may be freely used for personal research
2 CONT and by non-commercial entities as long as this message remains on all
2 CONT copied material. These electronic pages may not be reproduced in any format
2 CONT or presentation by other organizations or persons. Persons or
2 CONT organizations desiring to use this material for profit or any form of
2 CONT presentation, must obtain the written consent of the file submitter, or his
2 CONT legal representative and then contact the listed USGENWEB archivist with
2 CONT proof of this consent. The submitter has given permission to the USGenWeb
2 CONT Archives to store the file permanently for free access.
2 CONT http://www.rootsweb.com/~usgenweb.
2 CONT
2 CONT Submitted by: Rick Giirtman rickman@worldpath.net
2 CONT Date: July 12, 2001
2 CONT ****************************************************************************
2 CONT
2 CONT In the name of God Amen. I Jacob Shut of the County of Muhlenberg and State
2 CONT of Kentucky being weak in  body but of Sound mimery do this 21st day of July
2 CONT eighteen hundred and seventeen make and publish this my last Will and
2 CONT Testament in the manner following. That is to say first I leave unto my
2 CONT beloved wife Elizabeth Shut the plantation whereon I now live. That is to
2 CONT take in the Orchard where the fence now Runs with the Stable, Farmyard,
2 CONT Meadow and pasture field. During her natural life. And unto my son Jacob
2 CONT Shutt, five hundred acres of land to his Share. One hundred acres out of
2 CONT William Faiths(?) Surveys and one hundred acres out of Moses Gipsons(?)
2 CONT Survey, Eastward of my plantation. And unto my son Abraham I will two
2 CONT hundred acres out of the same two tracts. One hundred out of each. The part
2 CONT wearon He(?) now lives. And my two sons to have my farming tools ***** and
2 CONT F**ming tools. After my wifes decease. My two daughters Mary and Susannah
2 CONT to have one hundred and fifty acres being now lying in Daviess County on the
2 CONT waters of long fall. To be divided between them. And the House hold and
2 CONT Kitchen furnature, beds, loom, and also hogs, Cattle and horses, to be
2 CONT divided amongst my two daughters at my wife's deceased. In Witness Whereof
2 CONT I the said Jacob have this day Set my hand and affixed my Seal.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Shut -Seal
2 CONT Witness
2 CONT John Plain
2 CONT John Plain Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Muhlenberg County
2 CONT November County Court 1825
2 CONT The foregoing last will and Testament of Jacob Shutt Dec'd. was exhibited
2 CONT into Court and proven by the Oaths of John Plain Jr., a Subscribing Witness
2 CONT thereto and John Plain Sr. the other Subscribing Witness thereto having
2 CONT departed this life the said John Plain Jr. & William Kinchloe Came into
2 CONT Court and proved the Signature of the said JohnPlain ** to be his own hand
2 CONT writing. Whereupon the said Will is admitted and ordered to be recorded.
2 CONT Att. Ch. F. W i n g -Clk
