1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Note:  Some of the information below may be slightly different from the DAR public database. (F D)
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Dennis Smith, born 1748 in Germany; died August 27, 1829 in Greene County, Pennsylvania. He was the son of 92. Dennis Smith. He married 47. Elizabeth Zook November 14, 1771.
2 CONT
2 CONT       47. Elizabeth Zook, born May 13, 1756 in Pennsylvania; died September 19, 1845 in Stonelick Twp, Clairmont Co. , Ohio. She was the daughter of 94. Peter Zug and 95. Mary Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Dennis Smith: Dennis Smith served seven years in the War of the Revolution. He was a sergeant in Captain George Myers' Company, Washington County Militia as shown in the Company return of November 2, 1781.(Penn. Arch Ser
2 CONC ies VI Vol.2 pg 167.
2 CONT
2 CONT This company was recruited from the northern part of Morgan Township and parts of the North T enmile adjacent to the present Greene County Line.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dennis first settled on land warranted to Job Walton, which he patented March 26, 1806 unde r the title "Patience," and situated near the North Tenmile Baptist Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Dennis Smith and Elizabeth Zook are:
2 CONT *   		i. 	  	Peter Smith, born March 15, 1775 in Washington, Pennsylvania; died May 06, 1848 in Washington, Pennsylvania; married Priscilla Cooper 1804; born 1787; died July 04, 1841 in Washington County, Pennsylvania.
2 CONT *   		ii. 	  	Elizabeth Smith, born 1776; died June 11, 1853 in Mongan Twp., Greene County, Pennsylvania; married Jacob Johns October 09, 1794; born October 01, 1762 in New Castle County, Delaware; died August 22, 1845 in Greene C
2 CONC ounty, Pennsylvania.
2 CONT *   		iii. 	  	Susan Smith, born 1778; married (1) Unknown Milliken; married (2) Unknown Clark.
2 CONT *   		iv. 	  	Joseph Smith, born August 16, 1779 in Pennsylvania; died January 18, 1826.
2 CONT *   		v. 	  	Dennis Smith, born 1783; married Sarah Unknown.
2 CONT *  	Notes for Dennis Smith:
2 CONT * Went to Missouri
2 CONT * 
2 CONT *   		vi. 	  	Sarah Smith, born 1785; married Jacob Meeks March 01, 1801; born September 03, 1777.
2 CONT *   	23 	vii. 	  	Mary Jane (Polly) Smith, born Abt. 1787; marriedThomas Iams, born Abt. 1783 in Washington County, Maryland; died 1843. He was the son of 44. Richard Iams, Sr. and 45. Eleanor Pottenger.
2 CONT *   		viii. 	  	Hannah Smith, born 1787; married James Huffman; died April 25, 1828 in Greene County, Pennsylvania.
2 CONT *   		ix. 	  	Catherine Smith, born 1788; married William Seals.
2 CONT *   		x. 	  	Christopher Smith, born August 26, 1790 in Pennsylvania; married Margaret Britt.
2 CONT *   		xi. 	  	David Smith, born August 19, 1792.
2 CONT *   		xii. 	  	Rachel Smith, born 1794 in Pennsylvania; married Unknown Foster.
2 CONT *   		xiii. 	  	Abraham Smith, born March 28, 1799 in Pennsylvania; married Elizabeth Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/r/u/n/Susan-E-Runyan/GENE4-0007.html#CHILD459778
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Wife of Rev. War veteran, Dennis Smith, she was the mother of the thirteen children: Peter, Elizabeth Johns, Susan Milikin, Joseph, Dennis, Sarah Meeks, Mary Jane Iams, Hannah Huffman, Catherine Seals, Christopher, David, Rachel F
2 CONC oster,and Abraham. She was the daughter of Peter Ulrich and Mary Zug. 
2 CONT --------------------
