1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Irene S. Rice, 91, the “cake lady” of Mount Pleasant Mills, passed into her eternal home on Nov. 24, 2015, at the Richfield Senior Living and Rehabilitation Center.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born July 11, 1924, in Lansdale, a daughter of the late Rufus and Nora (Swartz) Hager. On Oct. 31, 1942, she married Paul R. Rice who preceded her in death in July 19, 1998.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1950 the couple moved to Snyder County to operate a dairy farm.
2 CONT
2 CONT Irene was best known for her baked cookies, cakes and wedding cakes for more than 50 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Irene’s life touched many in her community and beyond. Her legacy leaves behind a godly influence. She will always be remembered for her generosity, kindness and faith in her God.
