2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/64138836/mary-yothers
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Yothers, 92, died Monday evening, Oct. 11, 1999 at Souderton Mennonite Homes, where she lived since 1988. She was formerly a longtime resident of Bedminster Township. She was the widow of the Rev. Abram W. Yothers, who died i
2 CONC n 1994.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Bedminster Township, she was a daughter of the late Samuel and Emma (Overholt) Trauger.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Yothers was employed for several years by the former Myers Foods Company of Plumsteadville and later worked several years in the laundry at Rockhill Mennonite Community in Sellersville.
2 CONT
2 CONT After she and her husband moved to Souderton Mennonite Homes, she was a volunteer there for several years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Yothers often accompanied her pastor husband on visitations and entertaining guests. She enjoyed gardening, canning and raising flowers.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a lifelong member of Deep Run Mennonite Church, East, in Bedminster Township where she was active in the sewing circle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services were held Oct. 16 in the chapel of Souderton Mennonite Homes, Souderton. Interment was in Deep Run Mennonite East Cemetery, Bedminster Township.
