2 CONT
2 CONT John H. Histand of 86 E. Butler Ave., New Britain, was pronounced dead on arrival at Doylestown Hospital, Friday, after suffering an apparent heart attack. He was 51. Born in New Britain Township, he resided in the Doylestown area
2 CONC  for his entire life, living for the past 18 years on Butler Avenue.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of the late Daniel and Nora Huddle Histand. He worked as a crop farmer and also was a school bus driver for the Hatboro-Horsham School District and the Central Bucks School District, driving sports buses. He was a m
2 CONC ember of the Pennsylvania Farmers Association and the Mid-Atlantic Soybean Association.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving with his wife, Kathrine Nace Roth Histand, and a stepmother, Fannie G. Histand of Doylestown; a daughter, Priscilla A. Heckler of Sanford, Fla.; a son, James R. of Westfield, Pa; four stepsons, Charles Roth of Red Hill, 
2 CONC Donald Roth of Stowe, Pa., Robert Roth of Claremont, N.H., and Jeffrey A. Roth, at home; four brothers, Herbert Histand of Perkasie R.D., Walter Histand of Bridgewater, N.J., Norman Histand of Glenwood Springs, Colo., and Robert H
2 CONC istand of Wycombe; five sisters, Lena Hunsberger of Perkasie, Mary Reinford of Telford, Mabel Detweiler of Blooming Glen, Nancy Kulp of Mohrsville and June Histand of Doylestown; and four step-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be at the Doylestown Mennonite Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT -- Doylestown Intelligencer, April 26, 1981
