1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/82554653/herbert-huddle-histand
2 CONT
2 CONT Herbert Huddle Histand - 77, of Souderton; formerly of Blooming Glen, PA passed away on Monday, November 14, 2011 at his residence.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the loving husband for 55 years to Florence (Gahman) Histand.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Doylestown Twp., PA to the late Daniel and Nora (Huddle) Histand.
2 CONT
2 CONT Herb graduated from Lancaster Mennonite High School, class of 1952. In his youth and young adult life, he worked in his father's business, Pine Run Farm Supply in Doylestown, PA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Throughout his working lifetime, Herb was a Truck Driver for V&J Derstine Trucking in Hatfield. He also worked as a groundskeeper for Whitemarsh Memorial Park in Horsham.
2 CONT
2 CONT After retiring, Herb worked at Walmart in Hilltown, Faulkner Ford in Souderton and also volunteered at the Souderton Care & Share Shoppes. He was an avid reader who enjoyed driving to Lancaster with his family and spending time wi
2 CONC th his grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Herb was a member of Blooming Glen Mennonite Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to his wife, Florence, he was survived by: Josephine Martin (Daughter) & husband, Conrad of Souderton, PA; Linda Mack (Daughter) & husband, Dale of Telford, PA; Lena Hunsberger (Sister) & husband, Lester of Souderton, 
2 CONC PA; Mary Reinford (Sister) & husband, Ernest of Souderton, PA; Nancy Kulp (Sister) & husband, Clarence of Shoemakersville, PA; Walter Histand (Brother) & wife, Dale of Marco Island, FL; June Histand (Sister) of New Britain, PA; 3 
2 CONC grandchildren - Amanda, Travis & Christy Mack.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by his daughter, Shirley Histand; his two sisters, Edna Breuil & Mabel Detweiler; his three brothers, John, Norman & Robert Histand and his step-brother, Ernest Histand.
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorial services were held on Sunday, November 20, 2011 at 4:00 P.M. at Souderton Mennonite Church.
