2 CONT PAX Germany 1961-64; employee at his father's feed store; co-owner and manager, garden supply stores, Horsham PA 1967- Bob Histand, the last Pax director, made a gift of 2 million dollars to support a “Pax-like” program of present
2 CONC  day youth. We have been working with Mennonite World Conference to develop a program.  At a meeting in April in Akron, PA Mennonite World Conference and MCC agreed to work together to develop something in the southern hemisphere 
2 CONC which would honor their gift. (PAX - Mennonite Central Committee) After Bob’s death, Sarah gave their large Pennsylvania farm to create a charitable remainder unitrust through Mennonite Foundation (an affiliate of Everence). Using
2 CONC  income from the trust, Sarah helped start tranSend, a one-year Virginia Mennonite Missions program that gives young adults a taste of mission work through service projects around the world. Sarah’s trust continues to support half
2 CONC  the cost of each person in the program. (Everence) Robert H. Histand was a Pennsylvania Dutchman who devoted his life to serving others. This highly respected businessman was a great friend and mentor to Border Concepts and a leg
2 CONC end in the tool industry. In early 2000, we asked Bob to design the best tools for the trade, which he accomplished. Much to our sadness, Bob passed away in 2002 just weeks prior to our first production run. Because of his dedicat
2 CONC ion and contribution of wisdom, spirit, time and heart, to both the industry and Border Concepts, we proudly offer the Robert H. Histand Signature Tool Series. (Border Concepts, Inc.)
