2 CONT
2 CONT David Henry Alderfer, 95, died Nov. 13, 2002, at Oak Lea Nursing Home in Harrisonburg, Va., where he had been a resident for three years. He was born Sept. 7, 1907, to Henry S. and Annie Burkholder Alderfer in Souderton, Pa. On Ma
2 CONC rch 27, 1932, he married Mary Histand. She preceded him in death on June 12, 1998.
2 CONT
2 CONT He worked in sales and marketing for Mennonite Publishing House in Scottdale, Pa., from 1927 to 1960, and was Pitkin County (Colo.) hospital chaplain and manager of the Hospitality Center, established by Rocky Mountain Mennonite C
2 CONC onference, in Aspen, Colo., from 1961 to 1971. He served on many church boards and committees and was a charter member of Laurelville (Pa.) Mennonite Campground Association.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1975, he and his wife retired and returned to Scottdale. In 1988 they moved to Virginia Mennonite Retirement Community in Harrisonburg where he was a member of Park View Mennonite Church.
