1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Carol and her husband, Larry, were the owners of The Country Workshop in Salem, Conn., from 1984 to 1990. Carol had distinguished herself as a decorative artist and teacher. She achieved the level CDA (Certified De
2 CONC corative Artist) in 1989 and completed the first of three requirements toward becoming a Master Decorative Artist. She had been teaching decorative painting both locally and nationally for 20 years. She authored three books on dec
2 CONC orative painting (featuring her own designs) and two with other artists. In 1999, she was the artist of the year for New England Traditions. Carol was a founding member and past president of the Connecticut Society of Decorative P
2 CONC ainters. At the time of her death, she was Presidential Advisor for CSDP. Her work is currently spotlighted in the Artist's Catalog, showing pieces from her newest book and the book itself. She has two pieces on display in the Dec
2 CONC orative Arts Museum in Wichita KS. Her first love, outside her family, was painting with her beloved "Carrot Crew." (obituary, Daily Press, Newport News VA)
