1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/60407616/susan-a_-ruth
2 CONT
2 CONT Susan A. Ruth‚ 95‚ of the Souderton Mennonite Homes‚ died Friday morning‚ Feb. 11‚ 2005 in the skilled nursing unit of the homes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born June 5‚ 1909 on a farm along the Branch Creek in Lower Salford Twp. Between Lederach and Salfordville‚ she was the youngest living child of Abraham and Susan (Alderfer) Landis. She attended eight grades in the nearby Garges S
2 CONC chool on Haldeman Road.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Henry L. Ruth‚ a native of New Britain Twp.‚ March 29‚ 1929. While he worked for her parents as a hired hand‚ they first lived with her parents‚ then in a house on the lane leading toward Salfordville Road. It was ther
2 CONC e that they raised five children and she lived until the age of 77‚ at which time the couple moved to the Souderton Mennonite Homes. They celebrated their 75th wedding anniversary March 29‚ 2004 and Henry's 100th birthday Jan. 7 o
2 CONC f this year.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Ruth and her husband were founding members of Finland Mennonite Church‚ where she taught Sunday school and summer Bible school. In the years following World War II‚ she developed a special interest in counseling displaced per
2 CONC sons with Russian and Ukrainian backgrounds. In 1957‚ she took into her home two motherless sons of one of these families‚ as well as several other boys who stayed a year or two.
2 CONT
2 CONT After her children were raised‚ she began working as an aide in the operating room at Grand View Hospital in West Rockhill‚ where her husband who had retired from farming‚ was also employed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maintaining a lifelong interest in singing and playing the organ and piano‚ she assisted in the worship at Finland Mennonite Church and in various venues at the Souderton Mennonite Homes. In her late 80s‚ she learned how to operat
2 CONC e a computer and maintained a wide correspondence via email.
2 CONT
2 CONT A memorial service was held on Monday‚ Feb. 14 at the chapel of the Souderton Mennonite Homes. Burial was in Finland Mennonite Cemetery.
