1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Yoder, -- Jost J., son of Jacob Y. and Veronica (Slabaugh) Yoder, was born Nov. 24, 1860, in Somerset Co., Pa.; passed away at the home of his granddaughter, Susan-Mrs. Glen Beachy, near Kalona, Iowa, Nov. 2, 1955;
2 CONC  aged 94 y. 11 m. 9 d. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His youth was spent in Pennsylvania, where he accepted Christ as his Saviour and united with the O. O. Amish faith, remaining steadfast to the end. .
2 CONT
2 CONT On Jan. 5, 1888, he was married to Susan Gingerich of Kalona, who preceded him in death on March 13, 1943. The first year of his married life was spent in Pennsylvania, then they moved near Arthur, Ill. In 1897 they moved to Howar
2 CONC d Co., Ind., and in 1910 near Kalona. From 1916 to 1940 they lived with Joel; later several years were spent in the homes of Ira Nissley, Henry Mast, and Rudy and Sally Yoder; the last six years he was cared for in the Beachy home
2 CONC  where he passed away. They had lived in matrimony 55 years. Their union was blessed with 2 sons (Noah, deceased in 1929, and Joel of Kalona). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Those mourning his departure are a son, 5 grandchildren, 29 great-grandchildren, and many other relatives and friends.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were conducted on Nov. 4 at the home by Will Yoder, Adam Miller, and Albert S. Miller. Burial was in the Peter Miller Cemetery.
