1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/199797283/jonas_miller
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 children
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses (1811)(second Amish and third white child born in Walnut Creek Twnshp Holmes Co Ohio-his sone Jonas M suffered from rheumatism at 17 yrs of age. For 56 years and 7 mo was unable to walk and was blind for 39 years yet he was 
2 CONC a shoemaker)
2 CONT
2 CONT Infant son (1812)--Peter (1813)--Mary (1814)--Jacob (1817)--Catherine (1819)--Sarah (1821)--Elizabeth (1822)--Christina "dena" (1826)--Susanna (1828)--Elias (1833)--Barbara
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	1788 Death: 	1854
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonas was the fourth child of ten children born to Peter Miller and Mary Stutzman. He married Catherine Hershberger. They moved to Holmes County, Ohio and lived near Walnut Creek. They were Amish-Mennonites. They had four sons and
2 CONC  six daughters; two children died single. One son, Moses J. Miller, also called Klein Mose or Glee Mose (Little Mose) was a leading minister in the formation of the Old Order Amish.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: "Anniversary History of the Family of John "Hannas" Miller, Sr. (ca. 1730-1798)" by J. Virgil Miller pg 49
