1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT In  1884 he [Jacob W. Peck] bought the fine farm near Meyersdale, known as the Abraham Saylor farm, and one of the highest priced farms in the neighborhood…. The farm contains one hundred and ninty-two acres, all under cultivation
2 CONC  except twenty acres leased to the Meyersdale Fair Association.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1876 Beers Atlas, Summit Township page 89, shows the current fairgrounds location with the name of Mrs. A Saylor. I suspect this is the wife of an Abraham Saylor who died Sept 4, 1864. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob W. PECK's daughter, Cora Alice PECK married John P. SAYLOR, son of Peter Miller SAYLOR and Barbara HOSTETLER.
2 CONT
2 CONT While doing research to find a Mahlon SAYLOR (son of Jonas SAYLOR and Caroline BITTNER) who married Mary BURKHART, I found that Mahlon's brother Henry B. SAYLOR had a daughter Margaret R. SAYLOR. Margaret married Carl R. CLAPPER. 
2 CONC Carl founded Clapper Building Supply.
2 CONT
2 CONT My daughter, Debra, and my cousin Rachel's daughter, Marua, are both attending Penn State this summer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Prepared by: Stewart R. (Rick) Saylor
