2 CONT Gospel Herald - Volume V, Number 31 - October 31, 1912 - page 494, 495, 496 Bender. - Bro. David Bender was born May 2, 1832, in Lancaster Co., Pa.; died at his home near Milford, Nebr., Oct. 10, 1912; aged 80 y. 5 m. 8 d. He was 
2 CONC married to Lydia Miller Jan. 29, 1855, who died May 7, 1873. To this union were born 4 sons and 4 daughters; 1 son and 1 daughter preceded him to the spirit world. On April 1, 1875, he was again married to Lydia Miller. Grandpa Be
2 CONC nder was a faithful and an active member of the Amish Mennonite Church, from his youth, and his place was seldom vacant. His death was caused by several strokes of paralysis, being confined to his bed but 2 days. With a smile, he 
2 CONC fell asleep in Jesus, where he so much longed to be. He is survived by wife, 3 sons, 3 daughters, 34 grandchildren and 16 great-grandchildren. Funeral services Oct. 12 at the East Fairview Church, conducted by Jacob Stauffer and S
2 CONC anford C . Yoder. Text, Isa. 38: 1, latter clause. "God in His wisdom has recalled, The boon His love had given, And though the body slumbers here, The soul is safe in heaven." By a grandchild.
2 CONT
2 CONT _____________________________________________ Son of Jacob Bender and Magdalena Brenneman. Father of Mattie, Leah, John, Mary, David, Emmanuel, and Amanda. _____________________________________________
2 CONT
