1 NOTE {geni:about_me} MOUNT HOPE — Milton V. Shetler, 79, 7499 County Road 77, Mount Hope, died Monday, May 28, 2018 at LifeCare Hospice in Wooster from injuries sustained in a bicycle accident. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Wayne County on Nov. 23, 1938 to the late Valentine L. and Anna R. (Troyer) Shetler and married Mary N. Mast on Nov. 12, 1959. She survives. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a member of the Old Order Amish Church. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to his wife, he is survived by children Amanda Shetler of the home, Felty (Ada) Shetler, Noah (Miriam) Shetler and Ada (Michael) Kauffman, all of Millersburg; Anna (Dan J.) Miller of Orrville, David (Martha) Shetler of
2 CONC  the home, Martha (James) Beachy of Sugarcreek, Daniel (Mary) Shetler of Mount Hope and Wayne (Leah) Shetler of Fredericksburg; 43 grandchildren; 25 great grandchildren; siblings Amanda (Eli) Bontreger of Clark, Missouri; Abe (Eva
2 CONC ) Shetler of Salem, Arkansas; Ada Gingerich of Clark, Missouri; Katie Gingerich of Greenwood, Wisconsin; Eli (Barbara) Shetler of Numa, Iowa; Levi Shetler of Clark, Missouri; Lizzie (Joni) Miller, of Stanberry, Missouri; Moses (Cl
2 CONC ara) Shetler of Clark, Missouri; Barbara (John) Bontrager of Hillpoint, Wisconsin, and Ella (Clarence) Bontrager of Malette, Michigan; sister-in-law Mattie Shetler of Greenwood, Wisconsin; and stepmother Lovina (Henry) Yoder of Wi
2 CONC lton, Iowa. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to his parents, he was preceded in death by grandson Anthony Lynn Shetler, brother Daniel Shetler, sister Lydia Miller, brothers-in-law Jacob Gingerich and Ammon Gingerich and sister-in-law Anna Shetler. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held Thursday at 9 a.m. at the family residence with minister Roman Miller officiating. Burial will be at the Hochstetler Cemetery near Mount Hope. Friends may call anytime after 10 a.m on Tuesday and anyt
2 CONC ime Wednesday at the family residence. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Spidell Funeral Home in Mount Eaton is handling the arrangements.
