1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Susie E. (Troyer) Yoder, 76, of 6466 Township Road 327, Millersburg, passed away peacefully at home on July 26, 2022.
2 CONT
2 CONT Susie was born on August 6, 1945 in Fredericksburg to the late Eli R. and Amanda (Hershberger) Troyer and married the love of her life, Crist S. Yoder on November 9, 1967. Crist preceded her in death on November 5, 2020. She was a
2 CONC  member of the Old Order Amish Church and had a heart for missions.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are her 4 daughters, Lizzie Yoder, of Millersburg, Katie (David) Mast, of Brinkhaven and Amanda (Willis) Byler and Ruth Yoder, both of the home; 7 grandchildren, Christina, Irene, Atlee, Ervin, Ina, James (special friend
2 CONC  Kate Yoder) and Suzy; brothers, Melvin (Lizzie) Troyer, of Fredericksburg, Milton (Fannie) Troyer, of Shreve, Jacob (Katie) Troyer, of Holmesville and Eli Jr. Troyer, of Fredericksburg; sisters, Fannie (Henry) Miller, of Frederic
2 CONC ksburg, Sadie (Andy) Schlabach, of Millersburg and Esther (Lester) Chupp and Ada (Joe) Miller, both of Holmesville; sister-in-law, Katie Troyer, of Millersburg; and special friends, Martha Hershberger, Esther Byler and Jim and Sue
2 CONC  Burkholder.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by her husband, Crist; her parents; brother, Atlee Troyer; sister, Lizzie Wengerd; sister-in-law, Kathy Troyer; and a brother-in-law, Levi Wengerd.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be on Friday, July 29th at the Andy Miller Jr. residence, 6420 State Route 241, Millersburg with Bishop Joseph Miller Jr. officiating. Burial will be in the Honey Run Cemetery. Friends may call Wednesday after 2:00 p
2 CONC .m. and anytime on Thursday at the Miller residence.
2 CONT
2 CONT Murray Funeral Home, Fredericksburg, is handling arrangements.
2 CONT
2 CONT Posted online on July 27, 2022
2 CONT
