1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Millersburg - Atlee E. Troyer 69, of 5957 Township Road 605, Millersburg, passed away unexpectedly from a heart attack on August 2, 2021.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born on May 20, 1952 to the late Eli R. and Amanda Hershberger Troyer. On November 1, 1973 he married Katie Stutzman who survives.
2 CONT
2 CONT Atlee was a woodworker and a member of the Old Order Amish Church where he was ordained as minister in 1976 and as bishop in 1978.
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to his wife Katie, he is survived by their three sons and six daughters, Nancy (David) Burkholder and Sara Ann, both of the home, Wayne (Miriam) Troyer of Millersburg, Mabel (Eli) Wengerd of Millersburg, Fannie (David)
2 CONC  Troyer of Killbuck, Susie (David) Miller of Fredericksburg, Miriam (Dennis) Raber of Millersburg, Perry (Rachel) Troyer of Holmesville, and John (Laura) Troyer of Millersburg; 24 grandchildren; brothers Melvin (Lizzie) Troyer, Mi
2 CONC lt (Fannie) Troyer, Jacob (Katie) Troyer, and Eli Troyer Jr.; sisters Fannie (Henry) Miller, Lizzie Wengerd, Susie Yoder, Sadie (Andy) Schlabach, Esther (Lester) Chupp, and Ada (Joe) Miller.
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to his parents, he was preceded in death by a granddaughter, a sister-in-law, and two brothers-in-law.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held at the home on Thursday, August 5, at 9:00 a.m. with Minister Wayne Miller officiating. Burial will follow in the Locust Hill Cemetery. Friends may call at the home after 1:00 p.m. on Tuesday and any 
2 CONC time on Wednesday.
2 CONT
2 CONT Miller Funeral Care – Walnut Creek, OH 330-893-2273.
2 CONT
