1 NOTE {geni:about_me} MILLERSBURG -- Rudy J. Troyer, 73, 6007 Township Road 351, Millersburg, died peacefully on Tuesday, Aug. 30, 2016, at his home after a brief illness. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born May 7, 1943, in Wayne County to Jacob and Fannie (Miller) Troyer and married the former Fannie Kline in December 1963. She survives. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a member of the Old Order Amish. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving in addition to his wife, Fannie, are children, Rosanna Troyer, Amanda Sue (Ivan) Hochstetler and Marlene Troyer, all of the home and Mary Ellen (Daniel) Hershberger of Sugarcreek; nine grandchildren, and six great-grandc
2 CONC hildren; sisters, Barbara (Alfred) Schlabach of Orrville, Anna Troyer of Fredericksburg and Erma (Roy) Yoder of Middlefield; brothers, Eli (Katie) Troyer, Sanford Troyer and Aden (Clara) Troyer, all of Fredericksburg, Noah (Barb) 
2 CONC Troyer of Holmesville and Jacob Jr. (Edna) Troyer of Apple Creek; a sister-in-law, Susie Troyer of Holmesville and a special friend, Mary Wilcox of Millersburg. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by his parents; a brother, Dan Troyer; sister, Amanda Troyer; and a brother-in-law, Roy Yoder. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be Friday, Sept. 2 at 9 a.m. at the residence, with Bishop Andy Schlabach officiating. Burial will be in the Stutzman (Troyer) Cemetery, Holmes County. Friends may call anytime at the residence. Murray Funera
2 CONC l Home in Fredericksburg is handling arrangements. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The family extends their sincere thanks to the staff of LifeCare Hospice for their kind and loving care.
