1 NOTE {geni:about_me} MILLERSBUG — Delilah Troyer, 68, 8830 Township Road 559, Millersburg, died Monday, Dec. 4, 2017, surrounded by her family at the home of her sisters, Mattie and Sarah Troyer, after a six-year battle with cancer. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born June 5, 1949, in Millersburg to Dan R. and Anna B. (Troyer) Troyer and was a homemaker, caretaker and loved to work with flowers. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a member of the Old Order Amish Church. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are her father, Dan R. Troyer; sisters, Esther, Lydia, Mattie and Sarah Troyer, all of Millersburg and Clara (Noah) Schwartz of Salem, Ind.; brothers, Harvey (Miriam) Troyer of Butler and Jonas (Dena) Troyer and Milton (
2 CONC Laura) Troyer, both of Millersburg; a brother-in-law, Leroy (Lydia Sue) Chupp of Springboro, Pa.; 36 nieces and nephews; and 45 great-nieces and great-nephews. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by her mother, Anna; a sister, Elizabeth Chupp; an infant sister, Emma; and a niece, Anna Chupp. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be Thursday, Dec. 7 at 9 a.m. at the Milton Troyer residence, 8814 Township Road 559, Millersburg, with Bishop Ivan S. Miller officiating. Burial will be in Wengerd Cemetery, Prairie Township, Holmes County. Friends 
2 CONC may call anytime at the Milton Troyer residence. Murray Funeral Home in Fredericksburg is handling arrangements.
