1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jonas D. Troyer 70, of 8862 TR 559, Millersburg, died from injuries sustained in an accident at his home on Wednesday, November 27, 2024.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born on November 24, 1954 to the late Dan R. and Anna (Troyer) Troyer. On May 28, 1981 he married Dena Bowman who survives.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonas was a retired farmer and a member of the Old Order Amish Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to his wife Dena he is survived by his children, Reuben Troyer of Millersburg, Anna (Travis) Hoover of Holmesville, Mary Troyer of the home, Atlee (Viola) Troyer of Millersburg, Ruth (Roman) Miller of Holmesville, Vern
2 CONC a Troyer of Millersburg, Samuel (Mary) Troyer of Sarasota, FL, Sarah Troyer of Shreve, Rachel Troyer of the home, Laura Troyer (special friend Henry Miller) of Holmesville; 8 grandchildren; 2 foster grandchildren; siblings, Esther
2 CONC  Troyer of Millersburg, Harvey Troyer of Butler, OH, Clara (Noah) Schwartz of Kentucky, Lydia Troyer, Mattie Troyer, Milton (Laura) Troyer, Sarah Troyer all of Millersburg; and brother-in-law, Leroy (Lydia Sue) Chupp of Conneautvi
2 CONC lle, PA.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to his parents, he was preceded in death by his sisters, Elizabeth Chupp, Delilah Troyer, Emma Troyer and a stillborn sister.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held at the home on Saturday, November 30, at 9:00 AM with Bishop Aaron Troyer officiating. Burial will follow in the A. Wengerd Cemetery. Friends may call at the home after 2 PM on Thursday and any time o
2 CONC n Friday.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Miller Funeral Care – Walnut Creek, OH 330-893-CARE.
