1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Fannie M. Troyer, 78, of 10459 Harrison Road, Apple Creek, passed away peacefully on Saturday, Julu 19, 2025 following a period of declining health.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT At the time of her death she was residing with the Dan J. Miller family at 4790 Township Road 629, Millersburg.   
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born in Wayne County on November 13, 1946 to the late Menno R. and Mattie (Weaver) Troyer.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT She taught school for many years and was a member of the Old Order Amish Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by her brothers and sisters, Abe (Emma) Troyer of Fredericksburg, Amanda (David) Miller of the home, and Dan (Anna) Troyer of Millersburg; sister-in-law, Amanda (late Jacob) Troyer of Gallipolis; 34 nieces and neph
2 CONC ews.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to her parents, she was preceded in death by step-mother, Iva Troyer, and a brother Jacob M. Troye and a sister, Lizzie..
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held on Tuesday, July 22, 2025 at 9:30 am at the former Maysville Fabric Store with Bishop Eddie P. Miller officiating. Burial will follow in Yoder Cemetery. Friends may call anytime after 2:00 pm on Sunda
2 CONC y and anytime on Monday at the former Maysville Fabric Store. Spidell Funeral Home in Mount Eaton is handling the arrangements.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The family would like to thank the Dan J. Miller family, Ohio's Hospice LifeCare and the neighbors for all of the help that was given.
2 CONT
2 CONT
