1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Amanda M. Otto, age 87, of North Canton, went home to be with the Lord on Monday, February 3, 2014.She was born in Hartville, Ohio, on May 1, 1926, to the late Noah and Lydia (Miller) Beachy. Amanda was a talented 
2 CONC seamstress who loved to knit and crochet and gave numerous quilts and crafts to her children and others throughout the years. She retired as a cashier from the Hartville Kitchen and was a long-time member of the Hartville Mennonit
2 CONC e Church. She was a wonderful wife and mother who only wanted the best for those she loved.Survived by children, Linda and Mike Devine of Dover, Wayne and Mariane of Canton, Ruth and Wyman Schlabach of North Canton, and Floyd and 
2 CONC Nancy of Ravenna; granddaughter, Olivia; siblings, Nancy (Willis) Troyer, Dan (Ginni), Joe (Carol), Al (Martha), Mary (Dave) Wileman, Marti (Eli) Miller; sisters-in-law, Mrs. Eli (Martha), Mrs. Vern (Erma), Mrs. Bert (Reba), Mrs. 
2 CONC John (Dorothy), Ms. Amanda E. Otto, Mrs. John (Dorothy) Otto, Mrs. Dan (Ruth) Otto; and many other relatives and friends. She was preceded in death by her husband, Abraham J. Otto on May 1, 1970, and by brothers, Nelson, Eli, Ray,
2 CONC  Vern, Bert, John, and Jonathon.Calling hours are Friday, 4 to 7 p.m. and Saturday, 10 to 11 a.m. at the Hartville Mennonite Church. Service is Saturday, 11 a.m. at the church, with Pastor Henry Shrock officiating. Final resting p
2 CONC lace will be in the church cemetery. The family would like to thank the staff of St. Luke's Lutheran Community for their loving care. In lieu of flowers, memorial contributions can be made to St. Luke's Lutheran Community at 220 A
2 CONC pplegrove Street N.W., North Canton 44720. 
