1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==brief biography==
2 CONT b. ca 1730, Europe
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT John SCHROCK was born in 1730 in Somerset Co., Pennsylvania. He died in 1797 in Somerset Co., Pennsylvania. Parents: Nicolas Klaus SCHRAG.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT also known as '''John Schrock
2 CONT
2 CONT ==family==
2 CONT m. (1) _____ Unknown, m. (2) Elizabeth Unknown. 		 Children by _____ Unknown:
2 CONT # John	b. 1754 	
2 CONT Children by Elizabeth Unknown:
2 CONT # Elizabeth	b. 1774	
2 CONT # Barbara	b. 1775	
2 CONT # Magdalena	b. 1776	
2 CONT # Christian	b. 1777	
2 CONT # Veronica	b. 1778	
2 CONT # Caspar		b. 1780	
2 CONT # Anna		b. 1784
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Elizabeth MILLER about 1771 in Berks Co., Pennsylvania. Children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Anna SCHROCK,was born about 1771.
2 CONT # Elizabeth SCHROCK,was born in 1774 in Pennsylvania. She died before 1806 in Somerset Co., Pennsylvania.She was married to David HOCHSTETLER in Somerset Co., Pennsylvania.
2 CONT # Barbara SCHROCK, was born on 20 Aug 1775 in Somerset Co., Pennsylvania. She died before 1817 in Somerset Co., Pennsylvania m. Henry Hoschstetler
2 CONT # Magdalena SCHROCK, was born in 1776 in Pennsylvania.
2 CONT # Christian SCHROCK, was born on 20 Mar 1777 in Bedford, Pennsylvania. He died in Oct 1834 in Somerset Co., Pennsylvania. He was married to Susanna MILLER in 1800 in Somerset Co., Pennsylvania.
2 CONT # Veronica "Freni" SCHROCK, was born on 22 Nov 1778 in Pennsylvania. Parents: John 
2 CONT # Casper SCHROCK, was born on 16 Oct 1780 in Bedford, Pennsylvania. He was married to Mary ZOOK in 1801 in Somerset Co., Pennsylvania.
2 CONT # Anna SCHROCK.was born on 30 Mar 1784 in Bedford, Pennsylvania. She was married to Joseph LANDIS on 27 Mar 1804 in Lancaster, Berks Co., Pennsylvania. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==comments==
2 CONT Date and place of birth have also been (erroneously?) reported to be:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1730 at Saales, Bas-Rhin, Alsace-Champagne-Ardennes-Lorraine (now Grand Est), France
2 CONT * 1730 in Somerset County, Pensylvania
2 CONT
2 CONT Date and place of death have also been erroneously reported to be November 24, 1796 at Walnut Creek (the site of which was first settled by a European American in 1809), Holmes County (which was established in 1823), Ohio (which w
2 CONC as part of the Northwest Territory at that time).
2 CONT
