1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Somerset County Star February 3, 1910
2 CONT
2 CONT Elias Gnagey died early Monday morning at the home of his son Jacob, in Summit township, on the farm where he was born, aged 78 years and 24 days. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral services were held in the Amish Church near Compton's Mill on Wednesday at 9:30 a.m. The interment was in the graveyard adjoining. Mr. Gnagey was the oldest member of the Gnagey family descendants of Christian Gnagey i
2 CONC n this section. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a son of Jacob and Veronica Hochstetler Gnagey, and was born January 10th, 1832. He was married July 10th, 1853 to Barbara, a daughter of Daniel Hochstetler. To this union 12 children were born of whom seven preceded him to
2 CONC  the grave.
2 CONT He is survived by his wife and five children: Seville, wife of
2 CONT henry J Opel; Jacob E.; Lydie, wife of Jacob D. Yoder; Daniel E. and Catherine.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/68955266/elias_gnagey Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCo
2 CONC py]: ''Oct 1 2024, 2:20:06 UTC''
