1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Obituary - 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Henry Hochstetler, youngest son of Henry and Susanna Hochstetler, ws born near Myersdale, PA, March 23, 1840; died at Des Moines, IA, Dec 21, 1930. He with his parents moved from Pennsylvania to Johnson Co., Iowa, in 1855 her
2 CONC e he grew to manhood and was married to Anna Mishler in December, 1862. In 1867 he with his family moved to Washington Co., Iowa, where he has since resided. His wife died April 5, 1928. To this union were born 6 sons and 5 daught
2 CONC esr, 4 of whom preceded him in death. The children left to mourn the death of Father are Mrs. Georgr yode,r Mrs. Katharine Doolittle, Lewis, John, Nicholas, Harvey, and Walter. Also 14 grandchildren and 15 great-grandchildren and 
2 CONC a host of near relatives and friends mourn his dath. At the time of his death he was being cared for in his home by his granddaughter Anna Mathews, who by her untiring effort left nothing undone which would have added to his comfo
2 CONC rt and happiness, nor until his condition was such that he needed special medical attention did she reluctantl consent to his removal to the hospital. Though advanced in years,he has kept quite active and had a remarkable memory f
2 CONC or one of his age. He was conscious until the last, speaking to those at his bedside when he passed away. In his youth he united with the Menonite Church in which faith he was reared and lived his entire life. He was a good neighb
2 CONC or and citizen whose word was above question; quiet and unassuming, but firm and steadfast in the faith. He will be greatly missed in the community where he lived for 62 years. Funeral srevices were held at Des Moines, Iowa, condu
2 CONC cted by Mr. Stutzman of the Brethren Church, after which the remains were brought to Kalona, Iowa, where final services were held from the Christian church, Dec. 26, and the body laid to rest in the family lot in the Kalona Cemete
2 CONC ry.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/89821511/john_henry_hochstetler Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 28 2024, 18:48:50 UTC''
