2 CONT Services will be Friday at 9 a.m. at the residence, with Bishop Dan Hershberger officiating. Burial will be in Yoder Cemetery, East Union Township.
2 CONT
2 CONT Friends may call anytime at the residence. Murray Funeral Home in Fredericksburg is handling arrangements.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born Jan. 9, 1929, in Wayne County, the son of the late Pete and Katie (Swartzentruber) Gingerich, and married Mary Miller on Dec. 9, 1954. She survives.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elam was engaged in farming and was a member of the Old Order Amish.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving in addition to his wife, are children, Jacob (Rebecca) Gingerich of Loyal, Wis., Iva (Levi) Hershberger of Dalton, Susie Gingerich of the home, Gideon (Mattie) Gingerich of Fredericksburg, Andrew (Soloma) Gingerich of Pe
2 CONC ebles, Jonas (Mary) Gingerich of Apple Creek, Lovina (Dan) Hershberger of Dalton, Katie (Menno) Hershberger of Apple Creek, Levi (Amanda) Gingerich and Esther (Ammon) Stutzman, both of Dalton, Amos (Mary) Gingerich of Heuvelton, N
2 CONC .Y., and Rebecca (Dan) Stutzman of the home; 104 grandchildren; nine great-grandchildren; and a sister, Mary Hershberger of Wooster.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by a son, Joe; three brothers; two sisters; five half-brothers; and three half-sisters.
