1 NOTE {geni:about_me} APPLE CREEK -- Daniel E. "Elam Dan" Swartzentruber, 83, 6606 Mount Hope Road, Apple Creek, died Wednesday, Aug. 22, 2012, at his home.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Millersburg on April 7, 1929 to the late Elam D. and Mary L. (Hershberger) Swartzentruber and married Ada M. Shetler on Jan. 2, 1958. She survives.
2 CONT
2 CONT He retired from the pallet business and was a member of the Old Order Amish Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving in addition to his wife, are sons, David (Marie) of Apple Creek, Dennis (Angie) of Sarasota, Fla., and Norman (Diane) of Dover; a granddaughter, Wilma; seven step-grandchildren; nine step-great grandchildren; brothers, E
2 CONC li of Canada, Joe of New York and Elam of Millersburg; and sisters, Mary and Lovina Swartzentruber of Millersburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to his parents, he was preceded in death by brothers, Abe and Levi; sisters, Katie, Susan and Elizabeth; and a step-great granddaughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be Friday at 9 a.m. at the Eli E. Swartzentruber residence, 7977 Township Road 654, Millersburg, with Bishop Eli J. Miller officiating. Burial will be in the Yutzy Cemetery, Paint Township, Holmes County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Friends may call anytime at the Eli Swartzentruber residence. Spidell Funeral Home in Mount Eaton, is handling arrangements.
