1 NOTE {geni:about_me} MILLERSBURG Elizabeth E. Shetler, 72, 7971 Township Road 654, died Monday evening, Feb. 9, 2004, at her home after a period of declining health. Services will be Thursday at 9 a.m. at the Elam E. Swartzentruber res
2 CONC idence, with Bishop Eli J. Miller officiating. Burial will be at the Levi B. Miller Cemetery, Paint Township, Holmes County. Friends may call anytime at the family residence. Spidell Funeral Home in Mount Eaton is handling arrange
2 CONC ments. She was born Feb. 14, 1931, in Holmes County to Elam D. and Mary L. (Hershberger) Swartzentruber and married John B. Shetler on June 19, 1980. He died May 9, 2002. She had made her home in Dunnville, Ky., and Conewango Vall
2 CONC ey, N.Y. She was a member of the Old Order Amish Church. Surviving are sisters, Susie, Mary and Lovina Swartzentruber, all of the home, and Katie Miller of Greenwich; brothers, Elam E. Swartzentruber of the home, Dan Swartzentrube
2 CONC r of Millersburg, Eli Swartzentruber of Norwich, Ontario, Canada, and Joe Swartzentruber of Conewango Valley, N.Y.; 11 stepchildren and numerous step-grandchildren and step-great grandchildren. In addition to her husband, brothers
2 CONC , Abraham and Levi Swartzentruber, died previously.
