1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mary E. Swartzentruber, 82, of 7971 Township Road 654, Millersburg, Ohio died on Monday, June 27, 2022 at her home following a period of declining health.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born in Holmes County on April 3, 1940 to the late Elam D. and Mary L. (Hershberger) Swartzentruber.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a member of the Old Order Amish Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by nephews, Gideon Swartzentruber and Eli (Barbara) Swartzentruber both of the home; a brother, Eli (Anna) Swartzentruber of Norwich, Ontario; a sister-in-law, Ada (the late Daniel) Swartzentruber; numerous nieces,
2 CONC  nephews, and friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to her parents, she was preceded in death by brothers, Abraham, Levi, Daniel, Joseph, and Elam Jr.; sisters, Katie, Susie, Elizabeth, and Lovina.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held on Wednesday, June 29, 2022 at 10:00 am at the family residence with Bishop Yost N. Hershberger officiating. Burial will be in the Yoder Cemetery, Paint Township, Holmes County. Friends may call anyti
2 CONC me at the family residence. Spidell Funeral Home in Mount Eaton is handling the arrangements.
2 CONT
2 CONT A special thank you on behalf of the family to LifeCare Hospice for their kind assistance.
2 CONT
2 CONT Posted online on June 27, 2022
2 CONT
2 CONT Published in The Daily Record
