1 NOTE {geni:about_me} MILLERSBURG -- Lovina E. Swartzentruber, 68, 7971 Township Road 654, Millersburg, died Tuesday, April 22, 2014, at her home after a three-month illness.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born in Holmes County on Nov. 19, 1945, to the late Elam D. and Mary L. (Hershberger) Swartzentruber and had lived all of her life in the area. She was a member of the Old Order Amish Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are a sister, Mary Swartzentruber of the home; brothers, Elam E. (Mary) Swartzentruber of the home, Eli (Anna) Swartzentruber of Norwich, Ontario, Canada, and Joe Swartzentruber of Conewango Valley, N.Y.; a brother-in-la
2 CONC w, Dan Miller of Greenwich; and a sister-in-law, Ada Swartzentruber of Apple Creek.
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to her parents, she was preceded in death by brothers, Abraham, Levi and Dan Swartentruber; and sisters Katie Miller, Elizabeth Shetler and Susie Swartentruber.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be Friday at 10 a.m. at the family residence, with Bishop Eli J. Miller officiating. Burial will be in the Yoder Cemetery, Paint Township, Holmes County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Friends may call anytime at the residence. Spidell Funeral Home in Mount Eaton is handling arrangements.
