1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} APPLE CREEK -- Ezra J. Wengerd, 90, 2596 S. Swinehart Road, Apple Creek, died Monday, Jan. 6, 2014, at his home after a three-month illness.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Wayne County on Nov. 13, 1923, to the late Joe C. and Saloma (Swartzentruber) Wengerd and had lived most of his life in Wayne County. He was a retired day laborer and a member of the Old Order Amish Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Jan. 24, 1946, he married Fannie Bowman. She survives. Also surviving are sons, Harvey (Elizabeth) Wengerd of Ontario, Canada, Joe (Katie) Wengerd of Canton, Raymond (Mary) Wengerd of Apple Creek, Eli (Sarah) Wengerd of Guys Mi
2 CONC lls, Pa., Ezra Jr. (Esther) Wengerd of Gambier, Alvin (Margaret) Wengerd of Apple Creek, Henry (Ella) Wengerd of Fredericksburg and Reuben (Barbara) Wengerd of Apple Creek; 40 grandchildren; 36 great-grandchildren; four step-grand
2 CONC children; and many, many friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to his parents, he was preceded in death by a son, Dannie; a grandson; eight sisters; and five brothers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be Wednesday at 9 a.m. at the Reuben Wengerd residence, 9779 Hackett Road, Apple Creek, with Bishop Enos Miller officiating. Burial will in the Erb Cemetery, East Union Township.
2 CONT
2 CONT Friends may call anytime at the Reuben Wengerd residence. Spidell Funeral Home in Mount Eaton is handling arrangements.
