1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Some report her as Fannie (Feronica) Yoder
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT [   https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/82206331/veronica-b_-miller]   
2 CONT
2 CONT Freny was the sixth child of eleven children born to Christian G. Yoder and Barbara Y. Beiler. She married John "Hannes" Miller, Jr. in 1774 in Somerset, Pennsylvania. They had eleven children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Yost Daniel David Catherine Miller Hochstetler Jacob John III Elizabeth Isaac Emanuel Solomon Elias
2 CONT
2 CONT The last two children died single. The children who raised families all married into families with Amish-Mennonite names, nine in all. Four married Yoders, three married Troyer's, one married a Hochstetler, two married Beachy's, a
2 CONC nd one married a Gnagey. Some of course, were second or even third marriages. It was unusual that all of them moved to Ohio and stayed with the Amish-Mennonite Church. Hannes Jr., and Freny had ninety-seven grandchildren who raise
2 CONC d families. When John Miller Jr. died, his farm was sold to Abraham Miller, son of his brother Peter. There are no remaining stones marking the graves of Hannes, Jr., and wife Freny, but it is almost certain that they are buried t
2 CONC here, according to family custom.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: "Anniversary History of the Family of John "Hannas" Miller, Sr. (ca. 1730-1798)" by J. Virgil Miller pgs 33-38
