1 NOTE {geni:about_me} GREENWOOD, Ark.  Services for Nora Plank, 90, Greenwood, are 10 a.m. Monday at McConnell Funeral Home Chapel, Greenwood, the Rev. Eddie Wilson officiating.  Burial is 3 p.m. at Rosedale Cemetery, Ada, Okla.  Visita
2 CONC tion is 1-9 p.m. Sunday at McConnell Funeral Home.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Plank died Oct. 13, 2005, at Greenwood.  She was born Aug. 20, 1915, near Millersburg, Ohio, to John and Benah Troyer.  She worked many years at Meadowlark Homestead and the Corner Lunch, Newton, Kan.  She married Levi J. Pla
2 CONC nk Dec. 2, 1937.  He died in 1994.  Mrs. Plank was a member of Harvest Time Tabernacle and served as part of the CARE sight group.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by her parents; and her husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include one daughter, Mary Tucker and husband Tracy, Greenwood; one son, Roger Plank and wife Mabel, McKenzie, Tenn.; two grandsons, Laverne and Eric Plank, Jackson, Tenn.; four granddaughters, Shannon Buckelew, Greenwoo
2 CONC d, Hidie Loyer, Fort Smith, Ark., and Cassy Tucker, Memphis, Tenn; four great-grandchildren, Justice, Faith, Kristin and Grace; and numerous other friends and family.
2 CONT
2 CONT McConnell Funeral Home
2 CONT
2 CONT 24 SEP 2021, Notes for incoming transfer, sighted; added gender.  1) Bio section as written by the original creator of the memorial has been retained, and is below the divider.~
2 CONT Nora Plank, 90, lifetime baker and cook, died in her home Thursday, October 13, 2005, in Greenwood.  She was born August 20, 1915, near Millrsburg, (sic) Ohio to the late John and Benah Troyer.  She was the youngest of 10 children
2 CONC , and was told she was "very spoiled".  As an Amish girl, she would walk to the one-room country school with her brothers and sisters not far from their home.  Norra (sic) loved to bake and cook.  She worked many years at Meadowla
2 CONC rk Homestead and the Corner Lunch in Newton, Kansas.  Baking was just in her blood.  She was the best there is.
2 CONT
2 CONT December 2, 1937, Nora married Levi J. Plank.  They were married for 56 wonderful years.  Their love for each other and for the Lord made for a beautiful life together, Levi died 11 years ago at the age of 83.  Nora was a member o
2 CONC f Harvest Time Tabernacle, and served as part of the C.A.R.E. Sight Group encouraging others.  She loved her church and enjoyed the fellowship with them.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nora is survived by one daughter and husband, Tracy; one son and wife; two grandsons; four granddaughters; and four great-granddaughters.  She is also survived by many other relatives and friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT Viewing was from 1 to 9 p.m. Sunday, October 16 at McConnell Funeral Home in Greenwood, where the family visited with friends from 2 to 4 p.m.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral was held at 10 a.m. Monday, October 17 at McConnell Funeral Home Chapel, 137 N. Main in Greenwood, with Harvest Time Tabernacle officiating.  Burial was at 3 p.m. Monday at Rosedale Cemetery in Ada, Oklahoma.  Relatives an
2 CONC d friends were welcomed to come celebrate the home-going for Nora.  Nora believed she had been so blessed all her life, we are honored that she blessed so many of us with her life.
2 CONT
2 CONT Information was contributed to Find A Grave by Tonia Holleman , who has been on a project of documenting and photographing headstones in  Historical and abandoned cemeteries in Arkansas and Oklahoma.  If you have any additional in
